1
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:32,090
- Rufus Barron.
- I'm sorry?

2
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:34,850
- You are Rufus Barron?
- Why?

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:37,850
Do you have any identification, sir?
We're police officers.

4
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:40,450
We want you to come to the station.

5
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,090
Well, no, I can't.

6
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:00,330
Rufus Barron, I'm arresting
you for theft

7
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:02,130
and obtaining property by deception.

8
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:05,090
- You do not have to say anything.
- What am I supposed to have nicked?

9
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:06,980
The receipts
for the office lottery syndicate?

10
00:01:06,985 --> 00:01:08,495
Yeah, you wish.

11
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:30,970
- I'm grateful to you for coming.
- It sounded official.

12
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:34,290
Well, there are certain facts
in our possession.

13
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:36,890
Ah!

14
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:40,810
Well, to be candid, I had no knowledge

15
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,450
that Haughton was
using inside information.

16
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:50,770
I assumed that my future son-in-law
was trying to ingratiate himself

17
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:55,730
by getting me to sell my One-Way
shares and thus make a bit of money.

18
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:57,810
And did you, Joe?

19
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:01,290
Yes. A tidy sum.

20
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,450
I'm beginning to wish I hadn't.

21
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:07,570
Joe, it's your ex-son-in-law
I need to talk about,

22
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,570
not the Home Secretary.

23
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:11,730
Deed?

24
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:17,370
Hasn't he settled down?

25
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:20,100
He had an affair with a claimant
who was before him.

26
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:24,810
Impossible.
Deed is neither stupid nor corrupt.

27
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:28,210
- Fortunately, he found against her.
- Now she's complaining?

28
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,650
She is not.
That is hardly the point, Joe.

29
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:34,330
Lady everard witnessed the woman
leaving the digs.

30
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:37,140
Vera can't give evidence.

31
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:39,610
The Secretary of State,
the Lord Chancellor is loath

32
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,050
to have Deed sitting any longer.

33
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,700
He'll need the consent of both
Houses of Parliament to sack him.

34
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:50,530
Deed must do the decent thing.

35
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:55,010
These are the salient facts
in the case he heard.

36
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:09,610
I came to warn you
that the Lord Chancellor,

37
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:11,770
or whatever he may call himself now,

38
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:14,970
the Secretary of State
for Constitutional Affairs,

39
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:16,650
is gunning for you.

40
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,570
That sounds like fun.

41
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:20,530
He may have cause.

42
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:22,650
Did you have an affair with a claimant?

43
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:28,250
To have done so
would place you beyond the pale.

44
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:30,210
It flies in the face
of all we stand for.

45
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:32,810
I behaved foolishly, not corruptly.

46
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:35,650
Your brother judges
take a different view.

47
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:38,770
- Are they all against me?
- So it would seem.

48
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:44,130
- They want you to resign.
- I'd better take counsel's advice, then.

49
00:03:58,660 --> 00:03:59,690
Come in.

50
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:05,060
- Sir John Deed, miss.
- Can someone organise tea?

51
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:08,090
Yeah, sure. The resident judge's clerk
at Sussex confirmed you

52
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:10,250
- sitting for the last 10 days.
- Thank you, Tony.

53
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:11,340
Okay.

54
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:20,250
- You should sit permanently.
- I'm not as confident as you.

55
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:23,410
Jo, you'd be as smart on the bench
as you are at the bar.

56
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,610
I can't see them appointing me.

57
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:28,210
I was caught bunking off
from my last Judges' Seminar.

58
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:31,930
I don't think they'd be stupid enough
to hold that against you.

59
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:38,090
You did behave badly.

60
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:40,180
So, you think I should resign?

61
00:04:40,185 --> 00:04:42,130
Why does this always have to
be about you?

62
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:47,290
Why can't you just once think
how I might feel in all of this?

63
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,290
You asked me not to go away,

64
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:53,650
but right now I can't see any evidence
for why I should stay.

65
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:55,060
I just came here for some advice.

66
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:57,060
There you are, you see,
you're avoiding the issue.

67
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:59,980
I don't know why I didn't just go to
South Africa when I had the chance.

68
00:04:59,985 --> 00:05:02,050
Because you have two sons
and a career here.

69
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:04,010
Yes, John, and you!

70
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:14,970
- It's not like I don't want to change.
- Oh, come on, you're not stupid.

71
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,661
Judges are always being told
not to exist in ivory towers,

72
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:25,620
divorced from reality, to be humans.
Perhaps that's what you're after.

73
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,010
Can sleeping with a claimant
be regarded as human frailty?

74
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,940
I don't think my fellow judges
see it that way.

75
00:05:29,945 --> 00:05:32,215
Then clean up your act, John.

76
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:34,410
You could marry me.

77
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:38,730
Yeah, yes, I could.

78
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:45,420
But I'd need something more from you
than just an echo of a promise.

79
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:53,450
- You can't force Deed to resign, Ian.
- We might if we publicly shame him.

80
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:56,850
Be careful you don't put your department
out of sorts with most judges

81
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:59,850
rather than Deed.
They could close ranks,

82
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:02,210
particularly with the way
they feel about the executive.

83
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,050
Then we'll isolate him, Monty.

84
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:06,600
He shan't have another case here,
nor at the Strand.

85
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,890
We'll shut him out completely.

86
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:16,010
Well, there's a way to add pressure
and keep the judges on your side.

87
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:19,690
Peer review the case
where he allegedly acted improperly.

88
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:23,490
If his brethren find him wanting,
he'll have nowhere to go.

89
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,450
We'd need the right judge.

90
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:28,570
Michael Niven would
be at pains to be fair.

91
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:32,480
- And Deed meanwhile?
- Get him out of the way.

92
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:35,170
Find him something non-controversial.

93
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:38,890
Deed would find controversy
in a bus-lane violation.

94
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:45,970
A High Court judge is needed to lecture
at the Judges' Seminar at Warwick.

95
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:48,050
We could send him there.

96
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:55,690
Monty, my clerk tells me
that there's nothing for me to hear.

97
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:58,890
- Have we run out of cases?
- I wish that were so.

98
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:02,210
So, why is there nothing for me?

99
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:06,450
There's concern over whether you're fit
emotionally to hear cases

100
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:09,530
because of the indiscretion
with the claimant.

101
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:12,290
Am I tried and found wanting?

102
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:15,290
I warned Rochester
he'd need to be sure of his evidence.

103
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:16,530
Is he?

104
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,930
A number of the brethren
want you to resign.

105
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,730
Where do you stand, Monty?

106
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:25,730
Well, if it's true, John,
it shows a grave error of judgment.

107
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:38,970
Can we legitimately
peer review Deed, Michael?

108
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:40,810
I don't see why not.

109
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,660
We do it all the time
in the Court of Appeal.

110
00:07:42,665 --> 00:07:44,250
Will the judges support him?

111
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:47,330
Those I've spoken to
are furious with him.

112
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:50,290
He must stop hearing cases
until this matter is dealt with.

113
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:52,170
We can arrange that.

114
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:57,530
The Listing Officer's still saying
there's nothing for you.

115
00:07:57,620 --> 00:08:01,010
Does he have
any untried cases in that office?

116
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:03,090
When hasn't he?

117
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:08,340
Tell Mr Wilson I want him
to bring all cases awaiting trial here.

118
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:11,250
No, actually, I'll go myself.

119
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:12,770
Do you think you should, Judge?

120
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:22,100
- My lord, may I help?
- Why is there such a shortage

121
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:23,810
of cases for trial, Mr Wilson?

122
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:26,050
Are the Home Secretary's policies
so successful?

123
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:29,170
It's a shortage of suitable cases
for your lordship to hear.

124
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:33,040
This one? Donald Langham,
accused of decapitating a prostitute.

125
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:35,650
The resident judge has reserved that
to himself, my lord.

126
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:36,960
Date rape?

127
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:38,540
Mr Justice everard, my lord.

128
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:43,010
And the civil action -
Cardinal Waste Management PLC?

129
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:45,450
- That's not ready, my lord.
- I'll read the papers anyway.

130
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:49,770
But, my lord, Mr Justice everard
is to hear it after his rape case.

131
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:53,290
- It's far too dull for Vera!
- My lord, it's not ready...

132
00:08:56,900 --> 00:09:00,730
This could be an unimaginable nightmare
for local authorities.

133
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:05,650
If the claimants were to win this,
it could prevent local councils

134
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:08,730
from ever burning rubbish again.

135
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,300
That would be terrible, Judge.

136
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:12,840
It might prevent us
from producing so much.

137
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,970
No, Judge, people would
just chuck it anywhere.

138
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:23,170
I'd like all parties in court
tomorrow to hear submissions.

139
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:27,130
All rise.

140
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:37,850
Mrs Mills, I believe
I have an application from you.

141
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:43,690
Is this to be heard now, my lord?
We're not ready.

142
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:46,970
What is the application?

143
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:49,810
It's to order
Cardinal Waste Management PLC

144
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:53,170
to open their incinerators
at Peaks Farm.

145
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:56,290
- And the purpose is?
- So that the expert witness,

146
00:09:56,380 --> 00:10:00,370
the epidemiologist, can take
dioxin readings from the chimneys.

147
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:03,460
Dioxins are going into the atmosphere
and have seriously affected the health

148
00:10:03,465 --> 00:10:07,140
of both Mr and Mrs Peacock, who live in
what was their grandparents' cottage

149
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,810
adjacent to Peaks Farm.

150
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:12,250
These dioxins, we would argue,
have caused both of their children

151
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:15,010
to be born with teratogenic deformities.

152
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:18,400
The first child, my lord,
had its heart and lungs fused

153
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:20,570
and lived only a few hours.

154
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:25,300
The other, their two-year-old daughter,
Henri, was born with spina bifida,

155
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:29,370
no nostrils and only one eye,
as you will see in the photographs.

156
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:37,810
Yes, thank you, Mrs Mills.

157
00:10:39,420 --> 00:10:40,820
Mrs Channing?

158
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:45,370
We would argue that Cardinal
has fulfilled its duty to these parents.

159
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:46,890
All emissions found

160
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:50,410
were within the government's
permitted safety quotas.

161
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,100
How does the government know
what's safe?

162
00:10:52,105 --> 00:10:54,420
Ministers do not live next to the site.

163
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:56,330
Another issue, Mrs Mills.

164
00:10:56,420 --> 00:11:00,090
Further, my lord, the claimants
are now beyond the time

165
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:02,930
set at the pre-trial hearing
for exploring the site further.

166
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:05,370
Ah, that is a problem.

167
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:07,770
The claimants are funded
by civil legal aid, my lord.

168
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:10,500
You will be aware how scarce
funding from insurance companies

169
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:12,610
is for this sort of action.

170
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:17,410
Time limits exist to free defendants
from the threat of perpetual litigation.

171
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:19,850
Cardinal haven't exactly been helpful.

172
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:22,690
They're trying to stop us
getting to the truth.

173
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:25,610
We just want to know if they were
the cause of our baby's problems.

174
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,410
Yes, we understand that, Mrs Peacock.

175
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,090
We don't want this to happen
to anyone else.

176
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,610
- Yes.
- Mrs Peacock.

177
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:35,090
I will endeavour to find out
what the truth is,

178
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:39,890
whatever it is. But unless we follow
the correct procedure,

179
00:11:40,460 --> 00:11:43,221
however frustrating it might seem,
there is a danger that you could be

180
00:11:43,226 --> 00:11:46,416
overturned on appeal if you win here.
Do you see?

181
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:52,410
All right. Mrs Mills, are the claimants
close to acquiring additional funding?

182
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:56,380
There is another application
in with the underwriting insurers.

183
00:11:56,460 --> 00:12:00,090
We will need a substantial amount
of money to pursue this.

184
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:02,370
Is the epidemiologist
wanting to be paid for this work?

185
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:04,690
No. Most of the costs
involve shutting down the plant.

186
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:07,170
Perhaps Cardinal could help. Hmm?

187
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:10,170
My lord, that's hardly fair
to Cardinal shareholders.

188
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:12,930
Well, their rubbish may
have caused the problem.

189
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:15,850
No, I'm ordering
the site to be made available.

190
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:18,810
This is just an expensive
fishing exercise.

191
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,620
To shut down the plant,
costs?30,000 a day.

192
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,340
Which is a small price to pay
for peace of mind.

193
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:28,300
And that's what Cardinal and the local
residents will get if nothing's found.

194
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:33,210
So I want the case back in 10 days.
Mr Harrison?

195
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:38,420
Yes, my lord, that will be the 29th.

196
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,610
29th.

197
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:43,970
My lord, I would urge you
to reconsider this matter.

198
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:46,330
No, Mrs Channing. I have ruled.

199
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:51,610
I've managed to secure a case, Coop,
but I'm beginning to wish that I hadn't.

200
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:54,490
The pictures of that child
are harrowing.

201
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:55,940
Ah, John.

202
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:59,250
The DCA is pressing for you
to go to Warwick

203
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:01,410
to lecture would-be judges.

204
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:04,210
Won't I prove a corrupting influence?

205
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:08,970
I earnestly counsel you to go,
out of harm's way.

206
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:21,650
- Ian!
- Home Secretary.

207
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:22,770
How on earth is Deed

208
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:26,010
hearing the case
against Cardinal Waste Management PLC?

209
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,890
I understood it was in safe hands.

210
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,620
It was. Deed hijacked it.

211
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:33,420
It will return into safe hands,
I can assure you.

212
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,300
Can you be as sure
about the embezzlement case

213
00:13:35,305 --> 00:13:36,970
involving Sir Tim Listfield's PA?

214
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:41,210
Oh, yes. We're giving it to a recorder.
No one is more consistent.

215
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:45,410
I hope you're right. I cannot emphasise
enough how important it is

216
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:48,140
that this matter is resolved swiftly.

217
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:56,740
Matters are reaching crisis point
with you grabbing the Cardinal case.

218
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:59,090
I'm doing what I'm good at.

219
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:02,490
You're setting yourself
against your brother judges.

220
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:05,610
You're setting yourself above us.

221
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,940
There are rules and procedures
that govern jurisprudence.

222
00:14:07,945 --> 00:14:09,975
No one judges above that.

223
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:13,370
If you don't like those rules,
John, resign.

224
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:14,780
Our rules need changing, Michael.

225
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:17,250
We have a head
of the criminal justice system

226
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:19,100
who thinks he can interfere
when he wants to.

227
00:14:19,105 --> 00:14:22,695
And you're lending weight
to the argument. You must stop.

228
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:27,880
Go to Warwick
or the consequences could be extreme.

229
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:37,050
- John, you're only going to Warwick.
- Feels like Siberia.

230
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:40,010
- You don't have to go.
- I've got no choice.

231
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:49,460
Have I been insensitive about Michael?

232
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:52,650
He was such a gift.

233
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,730
What are you saying?

234
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:03,770
I don't know.

235
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:08,660
I think I'm scared that you might have

236
00:15:08,665 --> 00:15:11,775
missed your opportunity with him
because of me.

237
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:18,010
Oh... We think commitment
is going to change our lives,

238
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,330
that we won't be able to cope,

239
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:25,330
and all the time
that's what we really want.

240
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:30,410
Life-changing opportunities.

241
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:34,130
And that's what I want, Jo. I really do.

242
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:41,690
Well, we can't get him back
for our own selfish needs.

243
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:43,570
Are they selfish?

244
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:47,210
He's happy with his father.
I have to believe that.

245
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:01,850
I love you, John.

246
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:07,610
No matter what you do,
I will always love you.

247
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:13,690
Perhaps that makes me dysfunctional.

248
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:36,050
Barristers can't enter this way,
it's for judges only.

249
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:39,410
- I'm sitting as a recorder.
- Beg your pardon, Your Honour.

250
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:41,850
- Park in any of the bays.
- Thanks.

251
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:52,690
We have a very nice embezzlement
for you, Jo. Don't we, Peter?

252
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,610
- I'm only sitting for 10 days.
- Perfect.

253
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:57,370
The hearing is set down for eight days.

254
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:02,570
The evidence is straightforward.
Judge Lancaster was to hear it,

255
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:05,120
but his fraud case is running over.

256
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:09,290
I'll show you
what chambers you could use.

257
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:11,780
Thank you.

258
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:16,810
- Thanks.
- Judge Shakespeare's off sailing.

259
00:17:19,780 --> 00:17:22,610
Well, bet he doesn't like
his things being disturbed.

260
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:24,970
Well, he was
a judge advocate in the navy.

261
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:27,850
Doesn't put up
with any nonsense in court.

262
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:34,140
- Well, I'd best get reading, Judge.
- Ben, call me Ben.

263
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:36,820
Jo, we're a little bit short-staffed,

264
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:39,170
but I've asked Peter Wilson
to keep an eye on you.

265
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:42,290
But I'll be around
if you need any advice.

266
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:43,600
Thanks.

267
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:08,850
Mr Cantwell respectfully requests
that you know your place.

268
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:21,970
All rise.

269
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:39,690
Will the defendant please rise?

270
00:18:41,060 --> 00:18:45,170
Rufus Barron,
you are charged with eight offences

271
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:49,810
of obtaining property, namely money,
by deception,

272
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:55,890
contrary to Section 15 and 15A
of the Theft Act of 1968,

273
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:59,770
by using cheques
and false money transfers

274
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:03,610
to obtain from your employer,
Sir Tim Listfield,

275
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:08,690
the sum of?4.4 million.

276
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:11,810
How do you plead, guilty or not guilty?

277
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:15,940
- Not guilty.
- You may sit down.

278
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:20,530
Ah, Mr Cantwell.
Am I going to hear from you?

279
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:25,410
Yes, Your Honour. We would argue
that there is no case to answer.

280
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:29,730
All the money in Mr Barron's account
was, in fact, given to him

281
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:32,850
via transfers
signed by Sir Tim Listfield.

282
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:34,770
Is there evidence to support that?

283
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:37,130
Mr Barron's defence
is that he and Tim Listfield

284
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:39,530
were going to set up home together.

285
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:43,580
The?3.7 million was for that purpose.

286
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:45,250
I thought Tim Listfield was well known

287
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:48,370
for the famous women
he's frequently seen with.

288
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:53,330
The prosecution's case is
that the defendant stole?4.4 million.

289
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:58,090
The additional?700,000 has never been
traced to accounts held by my client.

290
00:19:58,180 --> 00:20:00,250
That doesn't mean he didn't embezzle it.

291
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:02,610
I think you know, Mr Cantwell,
that submissions

292
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:05,570
for no case to answer
are for a later stage.

293
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:07,810
Let's have the jury in.

294
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:11,410
Mrs Mcewan, how long have you been
Director of Human Resources at One-Way?

295
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,410
A year and eight months.

296
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:15,340
Were you responsible
for hiring the defendant?

297
00:20:15,345 --> 00:20:19,250
Yes, when I was personnel manager
at Whittakers,

298
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:22,090
the military communications corporation.

299
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:24,370
He came to the firm
about five-and-a-half years ago

300
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:27,570
as an accountant.
He was good at his job.

301
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,370
What was his job?

302
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:31,850
To bear down on costs.

303
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:35,010
After Whittakers was taken over
the new managing director,

304
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:38,010
Sir Tim Listfield,
found him very energetic.

305
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,740
Was there any
sort of sexual relationship

306
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,930
between Mr Barron and Tim Listfield?

307
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:44,370
No.

308
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:47,130
Mr Barron admired him
and was fiercely loyal.

309
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:50,130
But, then, Sir Tim inspires that.

310
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:54,010
There was
certainly nothing sexual.

311
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:57,890
Rufus may have fantasised
about such a relationship.

312
00:20:57,980 --> 00:21:02,130
But Sir Tim is quite
definitely heterosexual.

313
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:06,650
You know that
from personal experience with Sir Tim?

314
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:11,490
It's a legitimate question.

315
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:16,410
Well, Mrs Mcewan?
Did you have sex with your employer?

316
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:21,530
- We did have a relationship.
- A sexual relationship?

317
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:27,010
- Yes.
- Just so the jury recognises your bias.

318
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:30,900
Despite
your sexual relationship with him,

319
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:34,010
Tim Listfield
relied totally on Mr Barron.

320
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:36,850
He was closer to Listfield
than you ever were.

321
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:40,170
He certainly relied on him to keep
his financial matters in order,

322
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,210
but there was nothing
sexual between them.

323
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:45,020
Did you know
that Mr Barron was arranging

324
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:48,930
all sorts of corporate hospitality
for Tim Listfield and his associates?

325
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:52,900
- That would have been part of his job.
- Did you know that that included

326
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:56,760
paying prostitutes with whom
Listfield would spend the night?

327
00:21:58,900 --> 00:21:59,970
I don't believe it.

328
00:22:00,060 --> 00:22:04,290
Clearly, you don't know Tim Listfield
as well as you thought you did.

329
00:22:05,580 --> 00:22:08,330
Isn't it true
that he has vast appetites?

330
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:11,090
Sexual and material.

331
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:14,970
- Yes?
- Your Honour,

332
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:17,970
Sir Tim Listfield is
a well respected businessman.

333
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:21,010
This assault on his character
is hardly relevant.

334
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:24,410
Much of this case hinges
on one man's word against another's.

335
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:28,280
I think the victim's character
and history are very relevant.

336
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:36,370
Bisexual contact is not necessarily
excluded from those appetites.

337
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:39,810
Is it?

338
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,210
Mrs Mcewan?

339
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,570
What else is the judge
going to allow in open court?

340
00:23:03,660 --> 00:23:06,380
I'm assured the case is being
carefully managed, Tim.

341
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:10,970
That's not how it appears to me.
Why is Jo Mills sitting as the judge?

342
00:23:11,060 --> 00:23:13,250
She acted for a claimant
who sued my company.

343
00:23:13,340 --> 00:23:15,210
That's an entirely separate matter.

344
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:18,050
We don't want this
getting away from us, Neil.

345
00:23:18,140 --> 00:23:21,370
Perhaps it was ill-considered
to pursue this prosecution.

346
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:24,020
The CPS assured me it was open and shut.

347
00:23:25,620 --> 00:23:27,530
Let me talk to someone.

348
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:32,780
Why was this case given to Mrs Mills?

349
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:35,090
Temporary judges are usually amenable.

350
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:38,450
You could have given it to any recorder,
any judge but her.

351
00:23:38,540 --> 00:23:41,530
The government doesn't want this case
to become a political football.

352
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:45,450
Sir Tim Listfield is important to
this country for all sorts of reasons.

353
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:47,130
Defence being one.

354
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:51,050
We will get her on board, Ian.

355
00:23:58,260 --> 00:24:00,720
- Hello, Ben.
- How was your second day, Jo?

356
00:24:00,820 --> 00:24:04,700
- Well, like my first, nerve-wracking.
- But the evidence is straightforward.

357
00:24:04,780 --> 00:24:05,810
How am I doing?

358
00:24:05,900 --> 00:24:07,780
You're giving the defence
a great deal of slack.

359
00:24:07,785 --> 00:24:10,240
Cantwell will take advantage.
Rein him in.

360
00:24:10,340 --> 00:24:11,690
I'm sorry.

361
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:16,410
That bisexual tack, and the prostitute,
wasn't really evidence, was it?

362
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:18,380
No, I suppose it wasn't, but...

363
00:24:18,460 --> 00:24:21,730
Sir Tim Listfield
is the victim here, Jo.

364
00:24:21,820 --> 00:24:24,730
You shouldn't allow
any extraneous nonsense.

365
00:24:25,420 --> 00:24:27,650
I wouldn't want people to think
that you are prejudiced

366
00:24:27,740 --> 00:24:30,850
because of your previous
run-in with Listfield.

367
00:24:40,220 --> 00:24:42,010
Jo! A friendly voice.

368
00:24:42,460 --> 00:24:44,530
- Is it friendly?
- How are you getting on?

369
00:24:44,620 --> 00:24:47,530
It's like the Arctic wastes,
decidedly chilly.

370
00:24:47,620 --> 00:24:51,130
At lunch and dinner
my fellow judges hardly speak to me.

371
00:24:51,660 --> 00:24:55,810
- Did you Hear from MicHael?
- Not since his call to say he'd arrived.

372
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:57,300
You sound down.

373
00:24:57,380 --> 00:25:00,050
Oh, I hope you're turning out
better judges than me, John.

374
00:25:00,140 --> 00:25:01,690
I'm sure you're doing fine.

375
00:25:01,780 --> 00:25:03,940
I thought I was
until the resident judge took me aside.

376
00:25:03,980 --> 00:25:05,570
It's like being back at school.

377
00:25:05,660 --> 00:25:07,210
Just push back.

378
00:25:07,820 --> 00:25:09,530
I wish I was there.

379
00:25:10,500 --> 00:25:12,130
I wisH you were.

380
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:15,610
Listen, I've got to go.

381
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:19,970
I'll call you. Bye-bye. Bye-bye.

382
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:23,810
- Ah, sorry.
- She was heading through the wire.

383
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:27,850
If only we could all
shrink down to her size

384
00:25:27,940 --> 00:25:29,490
and escape for an hour or two.

385
00:25:29,580 --> 00:25:32,090
- John Deed.
- I know. Morag Hughes.

386
00:25:32,180 --> 00:25:33,400
- Hi.
- Hi.

387
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:37,170
Your lecture on sentencing
was pretty hard-hitting.

388
00:25:37,260 --> 00:25:40,170
Oh, good, good, good.
We have a Home Secretary

389
00:25:40,260 --> 00:25:43,370
who thinks the criminal justice system
is an anachronism.

390
00:25:43,460 --> 00:25:45,250
Can he be so capricious?

391
00:25:45,340 --> 00:25:48,130
Well, if only he was,
I could forgive him,

392
00:25:48,540 --> 00:25:52,130
but he panders to a sometimes
vengeful public, doesn't he?

393
00:25:52,220 --> 00:25:55,450
- Yet offending rates continue to rise.
- Are you surprised?

394
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:59,580
He favours a punitive system that
was seen to be useless 300 years ago.

395
00:25:59,660 --> 00:26:00,660
Oh!

396
00:26:01,580 --> 00:26:03,450
I have another lecture.

397
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:05,610
Bye.

398
00:26:08,940 --> 00:26:12,570
- Stay.
- Well, isn't it worth going to?

399
00:26:13,940 --> 00:26:16,370
You won't get your brownie points
if you don't go.

400
00:26:16,460 --> 00:26:19,250
No. I better had then.

401
00:26:35,500 --> 00:26:36,720
Hello.

402
00:26:37,860 --> 00:26:39,080
John?

403
00:26:41,340 --> 00:26:42,530
Who is this?

404
00:27:19,060 --> 00:27:22,370
Oh, sorry, Your Honour.
I thought it was an intruder.

405
00:27:22,460 --> 00:27:26,130
- I feel like one. You can lock up.
- Goodnight, Your honour.

406
00:27:26,700 --> 00:27:28,410
Could you walk me out of the building?

407
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:32,130
I have a horror of being trapped
in these places at night.

408
00:27:32,300 --> 00:27:35,250
Never remembering
all the codes to the locks.

409
00:27:46,100 --> 00:27:47,810
Sergeant Halesworth, when you searched

410
00:27:47,900 --> 00:27:50,490
the defendant's flat and office,
what did you find?

411
00:27:50,580 --> 00:27:53,170
At his flat we found
a whole wall of photographs

412
00:27:53,260 --> 00:27:56,370
of Sir Tim and Barron.
Most were of Sir Tim.

413
00:27:56,700 --> 00:27:58,690
Did he say why these were there?

414
00:27:58,780 --> 00:28:02,850
No, but we also found a number of
personal items belonging to Sir Tim.

415
00:28:02,940 --> 00:28:06,170
- Did he explain why he had these?
- He said Sir Tim had given them to him.

416
00:28:06,260 --> 00:28:08,610
Sir Tim said
he had simply mislaid them,

417
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:12,170
a pen, gold cufflinks,
monogrammed shirts.

418
00:28:13,100 --> 00:28:15,740
We also found a receipt for a Porsche,

419
00:28:16,260 --> 00:28:21,540
a jewellery receipt for two matching
designer wrist watches worth?44,000.

420
00:28:22,700 --> 00:28:24,650
A Spanish bank statement

421
00:28:25,140 --> 00:28:27,890
and correspondence
from a Spanish solicitor

422
00:28:27,980 --> 00:28:30,970
over the purchase of a villa
on the Costa Blanca.

423
00:28:31,060 --> 00:28:33,650
Did Mr Barron have the income
to support such spending?

424
00:28:33,740 --> 00:28:36,610
No, sir. He earned?48,000.

425
00:28:36,700 --> 00:28:41,930
We did trace?3.7 million
to accounts controlled by the defendant.

426
00:28:42,020 --> 00:28:44,210
The money had left
Mr Listfield's account

427
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:48,410
by means of money transfers,
transferred by Mr Listfield.

428
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:50,730
When we asked Mr Listfield about this,

429
00:28:50,820 --> 00:28:53,570
he said he wasn't aware
of signing these.

430
00:28:53,660 --> 00:28:56,090
Further investigation
uncovered two cheques drawn

431
00:28:56,180 --> 00:28:59,090
on Sir Tim's account
forged by the defendant

432
00:28:59,180 --> 00:29:02,330
for?300,000 and?400,000 in cash.

433
00:29:03,260 --> 00:29:05,650
We've yet to trace these amounts.

434
00:29:06,420 --> 00:29:09,890
The villa in Spain was expensive
by British standards.

435
00:29:11,180 --> 00:29:13,210
?550,000!

436
00:29:13,620 --> 00:29:17,290
Yes. All the floors,
some walls and the pool were marble.

437
00:29:18,220 --> 00:29:22,450
An expensive car,
matching designer wristwatches.

438
00:29:23,660 --> 00:29:26,490
Things that would not go unnoticed
in Mr Barron's life?

439
00:29:26,580 --> 00:29:27,930
No, sir, they wouldn't.

440
00:29:28,020 --> 00:29:29,650
Some of these items were purchased

441
00:29:29,740 --> 00:29:33,730
six months before Listfield's
allegations against Mr Barron.

442
00:29:33,820 --> 00:29:35,890
He obviously kept
his purchases hidden.

443
00:29:35,980 --> 00:29:38,370
When you pressed Mr Barron
about these purchases,

444
00:29:38,460 --> 00:29:39,610
what was his final answer?

445
00:29:39,700 --> 00:29:42,050
He said he'd bought them
for Sir Tim Listfield.

446
00:29:42,140 --> 00:29:43,210
He said they were in love.

447
00:29:43,300 --> 00:29:47,290
He used Tim Listfield's money
to purchase items for Tim Listfield.

448
00:29:50,100 --> 00:29:52,770
Why, then, was he charged
with theft and deception?

449
00:29:52,860 --> 00:29:54,730
Sir Tim had no knowledge
of the purchases.

450
00:29:54,820 --> 00:29:59,050
?3.7 million was
taken from his accounts.

451
00:29:59,580 --> 00:30:00,610
Sir Tim is a billionaire.

452
00:30:00,700 --> 00:30:03,450
A few million could be withdrawn
without him immediately noticing.

453
00:30:03,540 --> 00:30:05,730
You choose to believe
he had no knowledge of this?

454
00:30:05,820 --> 00:30:07,140
Yes, sir.

455
00:30:07,460 --> 00:30:11,130
Was there something inherently
more trustworthy about him?

456
00:30:11,460 --> 00:30:13,330
His knighthood perhaps?

457
00:30:13,420 --> 00:30:15,730
Does he have a proven
track record for truthfulness?

458
00:30:15,820 --> 00:30:18,970
- I would imagine he does, sir.
- You imagine, Sergeant?

459
00:30:19,060 --> 00:30:21,620
Is that a contradiction in terms?
An imaginative policeman?

460
00:30:22,820 --> 00:30:26,050
Mr Cantwell, amusing, but not relevant.

461
00:30:26,140 --> 00:30:28,600
Would you say Tim Listfield
was being truthful

462
00:30:28,700 --> 00:30:31,850
when he over-valued his company
in order to secure third-generation

463
00:30:31,940 --> 00:30:35,650
phone licences from the DTI?
Or when, on taking over Whittakers,

464
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:40,450
he promised all the jobs were safe,
then sacked 35% of the workforce.

465
00:30:40,860 --> 00:30:42,930
Your Honour, this really has
no bearing on the case.

466
00:30:43,020 --> 00:30:44,370
It might have.

467
00:30:44,460 --> 00:30:47,410
But only if Mr Cantwell
asks Sir Tim Listfield that question

468
00:30:47,500 --> 00:30:49,850
rather than this police officer.

469
00:31:10,780 --> 00:31:12,970
This judge is paying us back
for our past.

470
00:31:13,060 --> 00:31:14,610
I'd say she is.

471
00:31:20,460 --> 00:31:22,450
How long will I be here?

472
00:31:23,020 --> 00:31:25,130
They never specify, Tim.

473
00:31:25,220 --> 00:31:28,530
I got called yesterday.
Are you in the mugging case?

474
00:31:29,540 --> 00:31:31,810
I can't waste time here, Clive.

475
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:35,930
I'll speak with someone, boss.

476
00:31:43,540 --> 00:31:45,890
As the criminal justice system

477
00:31:45,980 --> 00:31:49,090
comes under increasing pressure
from government,

478
00:31:49,420 --> 00:31:51,930
the most contentious issue
that you will ever have to

479
00:31:52,020 --> 00:31:55,370
deal with as judges
is separation of powers.

480
00:31:57,740 --> 00:32:01,090
The purpose of the criminal law courts

481
00:32:01,780 --> 00:32:05,490
is to determine whether
a defendant is guilty as charged.

482
00:32:06,100 --> 00:32:11,250
Politicians should not and must not
play any part in that process,

483
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:15,250
and it's up to judges to resist
them when they try.

484
00:32:15,340 --> 00:32:19,330
This Home Secretary is
neither enamoured of the judiciary

485
00:32:19,420 --> 00:32:22,930
nor enthusiastic about juries,
while every day

486
00:32:23,020 --> 00:32:24,300
he's forcing through legislation

487
00:32:24,380 --> 00:32:28,130
that has the gravest consequences
for our civil liberties.

488
00:32:29,540 --> 00:32:32,850
We tend to acquiesce
in the erosion of our rights

489
00:32:32,940 --> 00:32:35,290
by our ignorance and indolence.

490
00:32:35,380 --> 00:32:41,210
So, the question I put to you is this,
how can judges hold the line?

491
00:32:41,300 --> 00:32:43,570
Is it up to judges to do that?

492
00:32:45,340 --> 00:32:49,930
In a democracy we elect politicians
to enact laws to make a safe society.

493
00:32:50,020 --> 00:32:53,690
In an ideal world, that would be
the case. But consider this.

494
00:32:53,780 --> 00:32:59,290
A parliament that is elected by
an ill-informed and apathetic public,

495
00:33:00,020 --> 00:33:03,450
will consist largely
of power-hungry self-interest.

496
00:33:04,500 --> 00:33:08,280
- Where does the fault lie, Judge?
- Well, with each one of us.

497
00:33:08,940 --> 00:33:11,250
We must all take responsibility

498
00:33:11,980 --> 00:33:14,010
for the fact that
certain elements of government

499
00:33:14,100 --> 00:33:18,250
are removing some of the safeguards
to effective protest.

500
00:33:19,980 --> 00:33:22,330
It's up to judges to stand firm.

501
00:33:23,580 --> 00:33:26,690
Can one man ever prove bigger
than the system?

502
00:33:27,780 --> 00:33:28,850
No.

503
00:33:29,940 --> 00:33:32,850
But he can provide an effective brake

504
00:33:32,940 --> 00:33:36,090
to a process that is
accelerating out of control,

505
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:38,930
and cause it
to be examined more closely.

506
00:33:41,380 --> 00:33:43,090
Any other thoughts?

507
00:33:45,780 --> 00:33:48,650
My concern is whether
the evidence from my wife

508
00:33:48,740 --> 00:33:51,410
would be solid enough to sanction Deed.

509
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:55,170
You really need the woman
he allegedly slept with.

510
00:33:55,260 --> 00:33:59,090
We'll risk what we have, Monty,
while the judges are with us.

511
00:34:02,580 --> 00:34:04,970
Mr Powell, how long have you been.

512
00:34:05,060 --> 00:34:08,010
Sir Tim Listfield's account manager
at your bank?

513
00:34:08,100 --> 00:34:09,450
Just over four years.

514
00:34:09,540 --> 00:34:11,370
So you'd know his signature,
we can assume?

515
00:34:11,460 --> 00:34:13,180
- Yes.
- Could you look at these statements,

516
00:34:13,220 --> 00:34:17,290
Lines 15 to 24, the money transfers,
and tell me who signed these?

517
00:34:17,620 --> 00:34:20,810
- Sir Tim Listfield did.
- And where did the money go?

518
00:34:20,900 --> 00:34:23,090
Into accounts controlled
by the defendant.

519
00:34:23,180 --> 00:34:26,050
Money freely given to him
by Tim Listfield?

520
00:34:26,740 --> 00:34:29,610
Sir Tim Listfield says
he knew nothing about them.

521
00:34:29,700 --> 00:34:31,530
And you believed him?

522
00:34:31,980 --> 00:34:33,380
Yes, I did.

523
00:34:33,900 --> 00:34:37,570
Then we come back to the question,
who is the more honest?

524
00:34:37,660 --> 00:34:40,090
Listfield or Barron?

525
00:34:42,820 --> 00:34:46,600
Well, Mr Barron did forge
Sir Tim's signature on two cheques

526
00:34:46,700 --> 00:34:48,810
for cash totalling?700,000.

527
00:34:48,900 --> 00:34:50,730
Thank you, Mr Powell.

528
00:34:57,260 --> 00:35:01,330
Unless you tell me what you did
with that?700,000, we're stuffed.

529
00:35:01,860 --> 00:35:05,330
- I can't tell you, Mr Cantwell.
- I can't defend you unless you do.

530
00:35:05,420 --> 00:35:09,050
Those two cheques for cash
remove all of your credibility.

531
00:35:10,460 --> 00:35:12,410
- I gave it to Tim.
- What?

532
00:35:13,380 --> 00:35:16,450
?300,000 and?400,000 in cash? What for?

533
00:35:17,700 --> 00:35:20,890
- Rufus, you forged his signature!
- He asked me to.

534
00:35:22,740 --> 00:35:25,610
- It wasn't the only time.
- Oh, so what are you telling me?

535
00:35:25,700 --> 00:35:30,090
He asked you to forge his signature?
Is he stealing from his company?

536
00:35:31,140 --> 00:35:32,250
No.

537
00:35:33,220 --> 00:35:35,650
He would never do anything wrong.

538
00:35:35,900 --> 00:35:39,250
He was so busy.
I had to run lots of things for him.

539
00:35:39,340 --> 00:35:41,330
Yes. Did he need cash?

540
00:35:44,300 --> 00:35:48,180
- I'm sorry.
- Rufus, you could go to prison.

541
00:35:48,900 --> 00:35:50,450
I can't say.

542
00:36:02,420 --> 00:36:05,610
It seems there was a culture
at One-Way whereby Rufus Barron

543
00:36:05,700 --> 00:36:09,530
would sign cheques for Tim Listfield
and draw out large sums of cash.

544
00:36:09,620 --> 00:36:11,890
- Is he saying what for?
- No, he won't say.

545
00:36:11,980 --> 00:36:14,770
Either he's protecting him
or he's scared.

546
00:36:15,500 --> 00:36:17,290
Either way,
I'd like to subpoena bank records

547
00:36:17,380 --> 00:36:20,130
back as far as Rufus Barron
taking over Tim Listfield's affairs.

548
00:36:20,220 --> 00:36:22,370
This is ridiculous.
You can't do that this late on.

549
00:36:22,460 --> 00:36:24,290
Well, if it helps us to find the truth.

550
00:36:24,380 --> 00:36:28,490
Our defence is that
Listfield gave Barron the money.

551
00:36:29,460 --> 00:36:33,090
The untraced?700,000
from cheques Barron forged

552
00:36:33,180 --> 00:36:35,820
was drawn
at the request of Tim Listfield.

553
00:36:35,900 --> 00:36:38,540
Finding further cheques
could corroborate that.

554
00:36:38,620 --> 00:36:40,170
Your man's a fantasist, Brian!

555
00:36:40,260 --> 00:36:43,290
With all fantasists
there's always an element of truth.

556
00:36:44,540 --> 00:36:48,650
- Is there enough to start this search?
- We'll only know by looking.

557
00:36:56,420 --> 00:36:58,490
I will adjourn
and let you search the bank records.

558
00:36:58,580 --> 00:37:01,890
- Judge, Tim Listfield is not on trial.
- No, I know.

559
00:37:02,580 --> 00:37:04,970
I'll pulverize that little rat.

560
00:37:05,060 --> 00:37:07,520
Someone's got to get a hold
of this trial, Clive.

561
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:09,370
I was assured
it would be straightforward.

562
00:37:09,460 --> 00:37:13,690
We can't stop the defence looking
at the records now the judge has ruled.

563
00:37:17,540 --> 00:37:19,690
- What did you get, Steve?
- The girls in MI5 say

564
00:37:19,780 --> 00:37:23,250
this judge is very emotional.
Lots of pressure points.

565
00:37:29,660 --> 00:37:30,770
Jo.

566
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:34,140
It would be as well
not to let the defence

567
00:37:34,220 --> 00:37:36,970
delve into Listfield's business affairs.

568
00:37:37,860 --> 00:37:39,700
It depends on its relevance,
doesn't it, Judge?

569
00:37:39,740 --> 00:37:42,330
Ben, we're all friends
on this side of the bench.

570
00:37:42,420 --> 00:37:44,530
Now, this is a clear-cut case, Jo.

571
00:37:44,620 --> 00:37:46,340
The money was taken
from Listfield's account

572
00:37:46,345 --> 00:37:49,020
- and ended up in Barron's account.
- Mmm-hmm.

573
00:37:49,100 --> 00:37:53,610
Keep the whole thing running smoothly.
Justice delayed is justice denied.

574
00:37:54,100 --> 00:37:56,130
Swift results are what we want.

575
00:37:56,220 --> 00:38:00,690
Now, my door is always open, Jo,
if you need any advice.

576
00:38:02,100 --> 00:38:04,930
That's what
the resident judge is there for.

577
00:38:29,900 --> 00:38:32,890
Just what does Rufus Barron know
about your business, Tim?

578
00:38:32,980 --> 00:38:34,300
Nothing very alarming.

579
00:38:34,380 --> 00:38:35,455
At the risk of repeating myself,

580
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:37,570
I don't think
this case should have been brought.

581
00:38:37,660 --> 00:38:39,730
Tough on crime? Isn't that your stand?

582
00:38:39,820 --> 00:38:41,730
It was still an unnecessary risk.

583
00:38:41,820 --> 00:38:46,450
Neil, he dipped his snout into my trough
and took?3.7 million.

584
00:38:46,860 --> 00:38:49,690
Perhaps he was relying on you
not doing anything about it.

585
00:38:49,780 --> 00:38:51,970
Then he'll get a big surprise.

586
00:38:57,780 --> 00:39:00,210
John, I've never felt so pressured.

587
00:39:00,300 --> 00:39:02,530
The resident judge clearly thinks
I'm going to mess up.

588
00:39:02,620 --> 00:39:06,170
Oh, everybody thinks
they know better than a recorder, Jo.

589
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:09,650
- Just keep pushing for the truth.
- He told me not to waste time.

590
00:39:09,740 --> 00:39:12,300
Hey, hey, come on! You're the judge.

591
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:15,290
Listfield is tHorougHly corrupt.

592
00:39:15,980 --> 00:39:18,440
Expose that and you lance the boil.

593
00:39:19,420 --> 00:39:23,610
- I wish I felt as confident as you.
- Look, just keep your nerve, Jo.

594
00:39:23,700 --> 00:39:25,610
Couldn't you come back
from exile and help me?

595
00:39:25,700 --> 00:39:31,090
Well, it seems that I don't have
very many friends at court.

596
00:39:31,940 --> 00:39:35,090
Those I do have,
have counselled me to stay put.

597
00:40:15,700 --> 00:40:18,690
I got a bag, don't worry. Thank you.

598
00:40:27,980 --> 00:40:30,570
- I have a message from Michael.
- What?

599
00:40:30,660 --> 00:40:32,610
He says he's still safe.

600
00:40:37,220 --> 00:40:39,490
Hey, wait. Are you all right?

601
00:40:44,780 --> 00:40:46,330
Did you see?

602
00:41:12,580 --> 00:41:13,930
- Hello.
- Is Marc there?

603
00:41:14,020 --> 00:41:15,930
Dr THompson's just going into tHeatre.

604
00:41:16,020 --> 00:41:17,660
Can I speak to him, please?
It's Jo Mills.

605
00:41:17,665 --> 00:41:20,095
I'll see if I can get Him for you.

606
00:41:25,140 --> 00:41:27,130
- Jo! How nice.
- Is Michael all right?

607
00:41:27,220 --> 00:41:29,860
- Yes, he's fine. He's in school.
- Are you sure He's all rigHt?

608
00:41:29,940 --> 00:41:33,210
Of course. You okay? Jo?

609
00:41:36,460 --> 00:41:40,290
Yes. Yes, I'm fine.

610
00:41:42,460 --> 00:41:44,410
I'll talk to you later.

611
00:42:05,060 --> 00:42:09,770
Your Honour, our search
of Tim Listfield's bank records

612
00:42:09,860 --> 00:42:14,370
has revealed some further 18 cheques
signed by Rufus Barron for cash.

613
00:42:15,500 --> 00:42:19,730
Listfield hasn't claimed
that any of this was stolen from him.

614
00:42:19,820 --> 00:42:23,490
We would like to offer this evidence
for examination by the prosecution,

615
00:42:23,580 --> 00:42:25,290
and expert witness.

616
00:42:25,940 --> 00:42:29,090
Your Honour,
I must protest this late evidence.

617
00:42:29,180 --> 00:42:32,330
If the police investigation
had been more thorough,

618
00:42:32,420 --> 00:42:33,930
they might have discovered this.

619
00:42:34,020 --> 00:42:36,330
Regardless, it's still too late.

620
00:42:54,660 --> 00:42:57,610
I will allow it.
How much time will you want?

621
00:42:57,700 --> 00:43:01,010
Well, 24 hours, I suppose.

622
00:43:01,140 --> 00:43:03,010
Is there anything useful
we could do meanwhile?

623
00:43:03,100 --> 00:43:04,820
I could get on
with the examination in chief

624
00:43:04,825 --> 00:43:05,730
of Sir Tim Listfield.

625
00:43:05,820 --> 00:43:07,970
Then let's get the jury back.

626
00:43:16,780 --> 00:43:20,530
I have never, I would never,
I could never allow Rufus Barron

627
00:43:20,620 --> 00:43:22,930
or anyone else to sign my cheques.

628
00:43:23,020 --> 00:43:25,930
Not only is it against the law,
under the Proceeds of the Crime Act,

629
00:43:26,020 --> 00:43:28,480
it would leave me
totally vulnerable to theft.

630
00:43:28,580 --> 00:43:30,330
It's a crazy notion.

631
00:43:38,060 --> 00:43:39,090
Jo.

632
00:43:40,420 --> 00:43:42,170
You shouldn't be letting
this evidence in.

633
00:43:42,260 --> 00:43:45,250
- But what he's found is relevant.
- Ridiculous.

634
00:43:45,500 --> 00:43:50,050
Sir Tim Listfield is not on trial here.
He's one of our leading industrialists.

635
00:43:50,140 --> 00:43:51,660
Now, get a proper grip on proceedings,

636
00:43:51,700 --> 00:43:54,530
or you'll be obliged
to discharge the jury.

637
00:44:00,300 --> 00:44:03,050
Why should the jury be discharged?
How can it?

638
00:44:03,140 --> 00:44:06,170
I think it's Listfield.
You know how well connected he is.

639
00:44:06,260 --> 00:44:10,220
- The resident judge is supporting it.
- You're not making any sense.

640
00:44:10,820 --> 00:44:12,610
Is Ben hearing the case through you?

641
00:44:12,700 --> 00:44:15,530
Well, he's certainly trying to tell me
how to conduct it.

642
00:44:15,620 --> 00:44:17,490
Are you losing it, Jo?

643
00:44:18,340 --> 00:44:20,330
I thought I was doing all right.

644
00:44:20,420 --> 00:44:23,090
I'm doing what you suggested,
putting pressure on Listfield.

645
00:44:23,180 --> 00:44:25,900
But it's gone wrong.

646
00:44:26,540 --> 00:44:28,930
Then fight back. I'll help.

647
00:44:30,300 --> 00:44:32,370
Let me see tHis evidence
tHat Cantwell's found.

648
00:44:32,460 --> 00:44:34,690
- Would you, John?
- Yes, of course.

649
00:44:34,780 --> 00:44:36,130
Thank you.

650
00:44:37,100 --> 00:44:39,090
Did you Hear from MicHael?

651
00:44:41,860 --> 00:44:44,850
Something strange happened
in the marketplace.

652
00:44:45,900 --> 00:44:48,290
A man said that Michael was safe.

653
00:44:48,940 --> 00:44:50,490
- WHat sort of man?
- I don't know.

654
00:44:50,580 --> 00:44:52,010
It was weird.

655
00:44:52,660 --> 00:44:55,490
Good evening, Your Honour.
Just checking.

656
00:44:56,940 --> 00:44:59,460
- Jo, are you all rigHt?
- Yeah, I'm fine, I'm just a bit jumpy.

657
00:44:59,465 --> 00:45:01,495
It was the security guard.

658
00:45:02,020 --> 00:45:03,240
Is Michael all right?

659
00:45:03,340 --> 00:45:05,290
Yes, yes, he's having a great time.

660
00:45:06,620 --> 00:45:08,610
He really likes His Half brotHers.

661
00:45:08,700 --> 00:45:10,450
Oh, that's good.

662
00:45:10,540 --> 00:45:11,690
I do miss him though.

663
00:45:11,780 --> 00:45:13,130
Yeah.

664
00:45:14,300 --> 00:45:15,810
Let me see the new evidence.

665
00:45:15,900 --> 00:45:18,810
All right. Thanks, John. Bye-bye.

666
00:46:00,900 --> 00:46:03,330
- Can I help you?
- Sorry to disturb you, Mrs Mills.

667
00:46:03,420 --> 00:46:06,210
Henderson is my name.
Could you come with us?

668
00:46:06,300 --> 00:46:09,330
It's a matter that concerns
national security.

669
00:46:09,660 --> 00:46:11,060
What do you mean?

670
00:46:11,140 --> 00:46:13,130
If you don't mind, madam.

671
00:46:28,340 --> 00:46:31,210
Would you mind telling me
where we're going?

672
00:46:31,420 --> 00:46:33,450
I'm not at liberty to say.

673
00:46:35,100 --> 00:46:37,530
Could I see your ID again, please?

674
00:46:47,500 --> 00:46:49,570
Excuse me.

675
00:46:51,220 --> 00:46:52,570
- Jo.
- John.

676
00:46:56,020 --> 00:46:58,010
Jo?

677
00:47:05,660 --> 00:47:07,650
Do you want to try mine?

678
00:48:33,980 --> 00:48:35,530
Do you know where we are?

679
00:48:35,620 --> 00:48:37,810
I think it's time to explain.

680
00:48:38,380 --> 00:48:40,170
Exactly why am I here?

681
00:48:40,260 --> 00:48:42,170
Oh, that's not for me to say, Mrs Mills.

682
00:48:42,260 --> 00:48:44,570
Well, someone's got to tell me.

683
00:48:45,340 --> 00:48:46,850
In due course.

684
00:48:48,900 --> 00:48:51,540
It's depressing about your little boy.

685
00:48:54,900 --> 00:48:56,570
Michael, isn't it?

686
00:48:57,420 --> 00:48:59,170
What's happened? What are you saying?

687
00:48:59,260 --> 00:49:01,530
I'm just making conversation.

688
00:49:01,620 --> 00:49:03,570
How do you know Michael?

689
00:49:06,780 --> 00:49:08,530
You must be careful.

690
00:49:08,980 --> 00:49:10,890
Accidents happen. Look.

691
00:49:47,340 --> 00:49:48,560
Michael.

692
00:49:50,060 --> 00:49:51,170
No.

693
00:49:52,340 --> 00:49:53,770
Oh, my God.

694
00:49:54,420 --> 00:49:55,820
Oh, God.

695
00:50:32,860 --> 00:50:35,370
Did you get much from the lectures?

696
00:50:36,940 --> 00:50:40,820
The administrative judge advised me
not to socialize with you.

697
00:50:40,900 --> 00:50:42,250
Why is that?

698
00:50:43,220 --> 00:50:45,170
You mean you don't know?

699
00:50:47,660 --> 00:50:50,170
Yet you chose to ignore that advice.

700
00:50:54,460 --> 00:50:56,450
I think you're dangerous.

701
00:51:00,380 --> 00:51:01,860
I like that.

702
00:51:03,340 --> 00:51:04,560
Do you?

703
00:51:09,380 --> 00:51:11,050
Excuse me, Judge.

704
00:51:12,140 --> 00:51:13,360
Mimi.

705
00:51:14,820 --> 00:51:17,610
Something seems to have happened
to Mrs Mills.

706
00:51:17,700 --> 00:51:19,730
Mr Harrison said
she wasn't in court this morning.

707
00:51:19,820 --> 00:51:22,170
She's not answering
either of her phones.

708
00:51:22,260 --> 00:51:26,040
Has he checked with the police?
She might have had an accident.

709
00:51:28,580 --> 00:51:30,060
Hello, tHis is Jo Mills.

710
00:51:30,140 --> 00:51:33,130
Please leave a message
and I'll call you back.

711
00:51:33,220 --> 00:51:35,650
Jo, this is John. Can you call me?

712
00:51:43,740 --> 00:51:46,130
Judge, the administrative judge
is after you.

713
00:51:46,220 --> 00:51:47,850
- Oh, goody.
- John!

714
00:51:49,340 --> 00:51:51,900
I'd strongly advise against leaving.

715
00:51:52,500 --> 00:51:55,060
In fact, I'd go further.
There could be very serious consequences

716
00:51:55,065 --> 00:51:56,410
if you desert your post.

717
00:51:56,500 --> 00:51:58,770
I'm sure you'll find
a replacement for me, Alan.

718
00:51:58,860 --> 00:52:00,080
John.

719
00:52:24,980 --> 00:52:26,650
Jo! Jo!

720
00:52:27,540 --> 00:52:29,020
Jo, it's John!

721
00:52:36,140 --> 00:52:37,140
Jo!

722
00:52:38,820 --> 00:52:39,850
Jo!

723
00:52:45,180 --> 00:52:47,640
Jo, what happened? Are you all right?

724
00:52:48,700 --> 00:52:50,570
Are you all right? What?

725
00:52:53,700 --> 00:52:56,290
No, this can't happen.
I won't let it happen.

726
00:52:56,380 --> 00:52:57,890
We'll bounce them straight into jail.

727
00:52:57,980 --> 00:53:00,370
Who? They didn't give me
their business cards.

728
00:53:00,460 --> 00:53:03,180
- It has to be connected to Listfield.
- Stop it.

729
00:53:03,260 --> 00:53:07,450
When I saw that window plummet to
the ground I thought I was going, too.

730
00:53:07,540 --> 00:53:11,090
- They are not getting away with this.
- How are you going to stop them?

731
00:53:11,180 --> 00:53:13,941
But if they can do it to you,
they'll think they can do it to anybody.

732
00:53:13,946 --> 00:53:15,456
I don't care!

733
00:53:15,940 --> 00:53:18,050
They threatened Michael.

734
00:53:18,220 --> 00:53:20,540
- You are not gonna abandon this trial.
- Stop it, stop it.

735
00:53:20,545 --> 00:53:22,535
I won't let you.

736
00:53:29,740 --> 00:53:30,890
Hello.

737
00:53:33,300 --> 00:53:35,210
Yes, this is John Deed.

738
00:53:38,380 --> 00:53:39,730
I see.

739
00:53:50,700 --> 00:53:51,890
Uh-huh.

740
00:53:56,540 --> 00:53:57,610
Thank you.

741
00:53:57,700 --> 00:54:01,410
Stay very close on this one.
I want no stone left unturned.

742
00:54:02,660 --> 00:54:04,770
Yes, thank you. Thank you.

743
00:54:08,220 --> 00:54:11,170
- There is a Maurice Henderson in MI5.
- And?

744
00:54:11,260 --> 00:54:13,010
He's on sick leave.

745
00:54:14,860 --> 00:54:18,640
The building belongs to the MOD.
It's been empty for over a year.

746
00:54:20,500 --> 00:54:22,890
And there are no windows missing.

747
00:54:24,140 --> 00:54:26,410
There's full-time security
and CCTV cameras.

748
00:54:26,500 --> 00:54:29,330
Nobody saw you enter,
nobody saw you leave.

749
00:54:31,380 --> 00:54:33,050
There was nothing captured
on the cameras.

750
00:54:33,140 --> 00:54:35,490
They must have turned them off.

751
00:54:37,300 --> 00:54:40,690
They were on all night.
The police looked at every tape.

752
00:54:46,500 --> 00:54:49,010
I can't go through
with this trial, John.

753
00:54:49,100 --> 00:54:51,130
Yes, you can.

754
00:54:52,860 --> 00:54:54,530
I thought
they were abandoning the trial.

755
00:54:54,620 --> 00:54:57,490
It seems there's another judge
on the scene.

756
00:54:58,140 --> 00:54:59,810
Can they do this?

757
00:54:59,900 --> 00:55:01,570
I don't think so.

758
00:55:01,660 --> 00:55:03,570
We are finding out now.

759
00:55:04,740 --> 00:55:06,730
I've got to make a call.

760
00:55:10,300 --> 00:55:13,170
Neil, I'm the victim,
not the perpetrator.

761
00:55:13,820 --> 00:55:16,130
This is getting completely out of hand.
Do something.

762
00:55:16,220 --> 00:55:18,170
Hold on a moment.

763
00:55:18,540 --> 00:55:19,890
Pull over.

764
00:55:33,820 --> 00:55:35,770
Tim, what does this PA know?

765
00:55:35,860 --> 00:55:37,770
That's not the point.
Take this seriously.

766
00:55:37,860 --> 00:55:39,050
I am.

767
00:55:39,540 --> 00:55:42,020
As long as Barron doesn't know
why he was forging those cheques

768
00:55:42,100 --> 00:55:43,620
they can only incriminate him further.

769
00:55:43,660 --> 00:55:46,820
- He doesn't know wHat tHe casH was for?
- Of course not. He's a PA, that's all.

770
00:55:46,825 --> 00:55:48,855
Good. Let me call someone.

771
00:55:49,540 --> 00:55:51,530
I'll ring you right back.

772
00:55:58,220 --> 00:56:00,090
Ian. Neil Haughton.

773
00:56:01,380 --> 00:56:03,620
I'm led to believe Deed is
trying to take over this case.

774
00:56:03,625 --> 00:56:05,570
I know. It's not acceptable.

775
00:56:05,660 --> 00:56:07,260
Ian, this could threaten the government.

776
00:56:07,300 --> 00:56:09,530
I do understand, Home Secretary.

777
00:56:09,620 --> 00:56:11,690
We'll make sure it doesn't.

778
00:56:12,700 --> 00:56:14,650
Tell me, how?

779
00:56:16,700 --> 00:56:19,050
The right decision was
to abandon this trial.

780
00:56:19,140 --> 00:56:21,090
It's not my view, Ben.

781
00:56:21,900 --> 00:56:25,210
But this is not your case.
You can't take it over, John.

782
00:56:25,300 --> 00:56:28,450
Lord Merriman in Bolton v Bolton was
quite clear about that.

783
00:56:28,540 --> 00:56:29,730
I'm not taking it over.

784
00:56:29,820 --> 00:56:32,540
Mrs Recorder Mills is
still the judge of record.

785
00:56:32,620 --> 00:56:34,930
She's still there
for the interlocutions.

786
00:56:35,020 --> 00:56:37,660
I am a High Court judge
sitting as I would

787
00:56:37,740 --> 00:56:39,570
to advise a probationer.

788
00:56:40,100 --> 00:56:43,130
As much as I might enjoy
bringing Deed to heel,

789
00:56:43,740 --> 00:56:45,930
how do you propose it's done?

790
00:56:47,260 --> 00:56:49,330
You are the presider, Monty.

791
00:56:49,420 --> 00:56:52,690
- You have the authority.
- Only if he accedes to it.

792
00:56:55,060 --> 00:56:56,770
I'll speak to him.

793
00:57:00,500 --> 00:57:02,730
It's your flouting the rules
like this, John,

794
00:57:02,820 --> 00:57:04,170
that's put you beyond the pale.

795
00:57:04,260 --> 00:57:07,090
- I'm trying to uphold the law.
- That's not how it appears.

796
00:57:07,180 --> 00:57:10,090
A High Court judge should be
the very embodiment of the law,

797
00:57:10,180 --> 00:57:11,210
not put himself above it.

798
00:57:11,300 --> 00:57:14,930
There is political pressure
on this case and I won't have it.

799
00:57:15,020 --> 00:57:17,970
John, you're becoming obsessed
with corruption in high places.

800
00:57:18,060 --> 00:57:22,020
Sir Tim Listfield is not on trial,
nor is the Home Secretary.

801
00:57:22,100 --> 00:57:23,170
Maybe they should be.

802
00:57:23,260 --> 00:57:25,370
That's not for you
or Mrs Mills to decide.

803
00:57:25,460 --> 00:57:28,770
If you do, the rule of law
will start to break down.

804
00:57:29,220 --> 00:57:33,290
Oh, God, man. Do we have to kidnap you
to save you from yourself?

805
00:57:34,860 --> 00:57:36,890
Was Mrs Mills kidnapped?

806
00:57:37,220 --> 00:57:39,010
I believe what she told me.

807
00:57:39,100 --> 00:57:43,530
I've always found her too emotional
for the bar, much less the bench.

808
00:57:43,940 --> 00:57:46,580
If you don't stand back from this,

809
00:57:46,660 --> 00:57:49,090
I'm going to have to talk
to the Lord Chief Justice.

810
00:57:57,660 --> 00:57:59,370
Jo, we can do this.

811
00:58:01,060 --> 00:58:03,090
What if they hurt Michael?

812
00:58:04,700 --> 00:58:09,010
We can't allow ourselves
to be held to ransom in this way.

813
00:58:09,700 --> 00:58:11,100
If we do,

814
00:58:12,180 --> 00:58:13,850
the law is lost.

815
00:58:18,140 --> 00:58:19,410
Come on.

816
00:58:52,500 --> 00:58:53,980
With respect, my lord.

817
00:58:54,060 --> 00:58:57,730
Are you now hearing the case
instead of the learned recorder?

818
00:58:57,820 --> 00:59:01,370
No, Mr Sorrell, I'm sitting
as a winger, as is my right.

819
00:59:02,780 --> 00:59:05,530
Refer all points of law to Judge Mills.

820
00:59:08,420 --> 00:59:09,530
Mr Cantwell?

821
00:59:09,620 --> 00:59:13,890
Your Honour, the handwriting expert
has confirmed that the

822
00:59:14,620 --> 00:59:18,290
18 additional cheques for cash
were forged by Rufus Barron.

823
00:59:27,820 --> 00:59:29,450
Mr Cantwell, this could indicate

824
00:59:29,540 --> 00:59:32,530
that your client is involved
in additional crimes.

825
00:59:32,620 --> 00:59:36,010
No. We would argue there was a culture

826
00:59:36,100 --> 00:59:40,650
whereby the defendant was encouraged
to sign cheques on Listfield's behalf.

827
00:59:44,340 --> 00:59:45,820
Only if the jury agrees

828
00:59:45,900 --> 00:59:48,620
that the defendant wasn't
stealing from his employer.

829
00:59:48,700 --> 00:59:51,260
If you run this as part of your defence

830
00:59:51,340 --> 00:59:55,450
the CPS could be obliged to add
further charges to the indictment.

831
01:00:02,860 --> 01:00:05,250
Might I have a short adjournment?

832
01:00:05,860 --> 01:00:07,810
20 minutes, Mr Cantwell.

833
01:00:08,940 --> 01:00:10,530
All rise.

834
01:00:13,620 --> 01:00:16,010
Don't go there, Mr Cantwell, please.

835
01:00:16,140 --> 01:00:18,090
Don't ask me about those cheques.

836
01:00:18,180 --> 01:00:20,640
It's the only way I can defend you.

837
01:00:21,220 --> 01:00:22,735
It's clear the cheques
were forged by you,

838
01:00:22,740 --> 01:00:24,370
but we have to know
where the money went.

839
01:00:24,460 --> 01:00:26,170
Because it doesn't look good, Rufus.

840
01:00:26,260 --> 01:00:30,010
You were drawing out huge sums of cash.
It looks like you were stealing it.

841
01:00:30,100 --> 01:00:31,370
I can't tell you.

842
01:00:31,460 --> 01:00:34,610
Are you protecting
someone other than Listfield?

843
01:00:35,300 --> 01:00:38,130
Look, Rufus, having a love affair
and his giving you the money,

844
01:00:38,220 --> 01:00:40,650
it's a perfectly valid defence.

845
01:00:40,740 --> 01:00:42,370
It only falls down if you had the money

846
01:00:42,460 --> 01:00:46,210
from his forged signature
and we don't show where it's gone.

847
01:00:46,860 --> 01:00:48,490
I won't hurt Tim.

848
01:00:49,460 --> 01:00:51,410
No matter what he does to me.

849
01:00:51,500 --> 01:00:54,370
What he's doing to you
is ruining your life.

850
01:00:55,580 --> 01:00:57,170
It was a bribe.

851
01:01:00,700 --> 01:01:02,530
Over a business deal.

852
01:01:05,860 --> 01:01:07,890
Well, I guessed that much.

853
01:01:09,060 --> 01:01:10,330
Who for?

854
01:01:12,980 --> 01:01:14,650
I can't tell you.

855
01:01:16,220 --> 01:01:17,930
You mean you won't.

856
01:01:27,380 --> 01:01:28,970
Mr Cantwell?

857
01:01:30,220 --> 01:01:31,740
We are not going to pursue the culture

858
01:01:31,780 --> 01:01:34,850
that allowed Rufus Barron
to sign Listfield's cheques.

859
01:01:34,940 --> 01:01:37,660
I would instead like to
resume by cross-examining.

860
01:01:37,740 --> 01:01:39,410
Sir Tim Listfield.

861
01:01:41,540 --> 01:01:42,610
Sir.

862
01:01:44,500 --> 01:01:47,650
Do you know how much money
you have in the bank?

863
01:01:48,060 --> 01:01:50,250
Not enough for bloated rats to steal.

864
01:01:50,340 --> 01:01:53,090
Didn't you, in fact,
give Mr Barron the money?

865
01:01:53,180 --> 01:01:55,370
Why would I give him?4.4 million?

866
01:01:55,460 --> 01:01:58,490
Because he promised you
love and loyalty.

867
01:01:58,580 --> 01:02:00,330
Mr Cantwell,
you're either a complete fool

868
01:02:00,420 --> 01:02:02,730
or a fantasist like your client.

869
01:02:04,380 --> 01:02:06,170
Answer the question.

870
01:02:07,660 --> 01:02:10,570
A lot of people working for me
are loving and loyal.

871
01:02:10,660 --> 01:02:12,450
I treat them right.

872
01:02:12,540 --> 01:02:15,050
I don't give them
my hard-earned millions.

873
01:02:15,140 --> 01:02:16,770
All the money that went into accounts

874
01:02:16,860 --> 01:02:20,050
controlled by Mr Barron
was money transferred by you,

875
01:02:20,140 --> 01:02:22,250
that you signed over to him.

876
01:02:22,340 --> 01:02:25,690
What about the?300,000 and the?400,000
he forged cheques for?

877
01:02:25,780 --> 01:02:27,850
That money has never been traced
to the defendant.

878
01:02:27,940 --> 01:02:29,650
Well, he forged my signature.

879
01:02:29,740 --> 01:02:35,730
You badly used your vulnerable PA,
who was helplessly in love with you,

880
01:02:36,620 --> 01:02:40,530
asking him to hide away money
from the woman you were divorcing,

881
01:02:40,620 --> 01:02:43,180
under the pretence
that you'd run away together.

882
01:02:43,260 --> 01:02:46,250
You're talking about
nearly?4.5 million.

883
01:02:46,340 --> 01:02:48,420
I could have half the country
for that sort of money,

884
01:02:48,425 --> 01:02:49,450
if I was so inclined.

885
01:02:49,540 --> 01:02:51,020
Is that how you saw Mr Barron?

886
01:02:51,100 --> 01:02:54,330
As a commodity
to serve your sexual appetite?

887
01:02:54,420 --> 01:02:55,690
He stole my money.

888
01:02:55,780 --> 01:02:57,450
You are bisexual?

889
01:02:58,980 --> 01:03:01,290
Do I have to answer this drivel?

890
01:03:02,300 --> 01:03:05,490
You can simply say you're not,
if it's not true.

891
01:03:05,580 --> 01:03:08,930
Well, of course it's not true.
I've had three wives.

892
01:03:09,220 --> 01:03:11,650
That must mean something,
even in this cock-eyed court.

893
01:03:11,740 --> 01:03:14,890
Sometimes marriage is a means
to disguise the fact.

894
01:03:14,980 --> 01:03:16,690
You'll just have to take my word.

895
01:03:16,780 --> 01:03:19,850
Oh, I'm sure the jury
will happily take your word, sir,

896
01:03:19,940 --> 01:03:21,290
just as the DTI did

897
01:03:21,380 --> 01:03:23,450
when you inflated
the value of your company

898
01:03:23,540 --> 01:03:27,050
in your application
for third-generation phone licences.

899
01:03:27,380 --> 01:03:30,890
Just as the workers at Whittakers did
before you sacked 1400 of them

900
01:03:30,980 --> 01:03:32,380
after promising you wouldn't.

901
01:03:32,460 --> 01:03:34,570
But I did keep another 4000 in work.

902
01:03:34,660 --> 01:03:37,330
Sir, I put it to you again.
You are bisexual.

903
01:03:38,540 --> 01:03:40,370
The money you gave Mr Barron
was a nest egg

904
01:03:40,460 --> 01:03:42,500
for the two of you to set up
a secret home together,

905
01:03:42,505 --> 01:03:43,780
and to stop, I quote,

906
01:03:43,860 --> 01:03:46,290
"My money-grabbing wife
from getting it."

907
01:03:46,380 --> 01:03:48,020
I've reached a settlement
with my ex-wife.

908
01:03:48,100 --> 01:03:49,620
And once you'd reached that settlement

909
01:03:49,625 --> 01:03:52,730
you demanded the return of the money
you'd had Mr Barron hide.

910
01:03:52,820 --> 01:03:55,020
But he believed your story
that you'd run away together.

911
01:03:55,060 --> 01:03:57,130
He was serious about you.
He wanted to make it work.

912
01:03:57,220 --> 01:04:00,650
So you cast him aside and accused him
of stealing your money. Yes?

913
01:04:00,740 --> 01:04:02,610
You're as mad as he is.

914
01:04:02,700 --> 01:04:04,330
I'm heterosexual.

915
01:04:04,420 --> 01:04:07,290
I've never had sex with a man.
Not any man.

916
01:04:07,620 --> 01:04:10,370
And if I did it certainly wouldn't be
with a fat poof like that.

917
01:04:10,460 --> 01:04:12,970
Tim, I've lost weight like you said.

918
01:04:19,300 --> 01:04:21,050
Rufus, listen to me.

919
01:04:22,980 --> 01:04:26,410
Whatever you had
or think you have with Tim Listfield,

920
01:04:26,980 --> 01:04:28,300
it's over.

921
01:04:29,420 --> 01:04:33,200
- But I did lose the weight.
- Rufus, look at me.

922
01:04:40,100 --> 01:04:41,730
It's a fantasy.

923
01:04:43,300 --> 01:04:47,210
He doesn't give a fig about you
or your feelings. He never did.

924
01:04:48,220 --> 01:04:51,170
He'd happily see you
go to jail for 10 years.

925
01:04:52,620 --> 01:04:54,610
The only way that can happen
is by keeping quiet

926
01:04:54,700 --> 01:04:56,970
and not telling
about those two cash payments

927
01:04:57,060 --> 01:04:58,930
for?300,000 and?400,000.

928
01:05:05,300 --> 01:05:09,010
Rufus, can you imagine
what 10 years in clink will be like?

929
01:05:10,700 --> 01:05:12,490
It won't be pleasant.

930
01:05:15,060 --> 01:05:17,450
Stop protecting Listfield.

931
01:05:19,700 --> 01:05:21,930
Tell me where the money went.

932
01:05:25,460 --> 01:05:27,170
Will you tell me?

933
01:05:33,540 --> 01:05:38,090
Your Honour,
a matter of grave concern has arisen.

934
01:05:43,660 --> 01:05:45,810
Might I see you in chambers?

935
01:05:48,620 --> 01:05:50,250
All rise.

936
01:05:55,660 --> 01:05:59,570
Mr Barron said?700,000 cash withdrawals

937
01:06:00,660 --> 01:06:04,770
were a bribe for over-runs
on defence contracts.

938
01:06:07,900 --> 01:06:11,250
- Is there evidence of that, Brian?
- He says there is.

939
01:06:11,700 --> 01:06:13,370
Oh, it gets worse.

940
01:06:13,780 --> 01:06:16,450
The bribe was for a cabinet minister.

941
01:06:21,020 --> 01:06:23,450
That is a very serious allegation.

942
01:06:27,740 --> 01:06:30,380
It is likely to incriminate
your client as well as Listfield.

943
01:06:30,460 --> 01:06:32,370
I did warn him of that.

944
01:06:34,860 --> 01:06:36,850
Did he name the minister?

945
01:06:38,340 --> 01:06:39,530
He did.

946
01:06:45,980 --> 01:06:49,970
Only two items on your bank statement
remain unexplained.

947
01:06:50,940 --> 01:06:53,890
Only two items have any interest
to this court at the moment.

948
01:06:53,980 --> 01:06:55,930
17 and 24.

949
01:06:56,300 --> 01:07:00,410
Cash withdrawals
for?300,000 and?400,000 respectively.

950
01:07:01,980 --> 01:07:03,690
That's a lot of cash.

951
01:07:03,780 --> 01:07:06,210
Almost three quarters
of a million pounds.

952
01:07:07,260 --> 01:07:09,770
Can you tell us what happened to it?

953
01:07:10,140 --> 01:07:12,370
- No, I can't.
- Oh, you can't.

954
01:07:14,100 --> 01:07:15,580
Or you won't?

955
01:07:15,980 --> 01:07:19,010
Well, I assume my thieving PA took it
to fuel his fantasies.

956
01:07:19,100 --> 01:07:21,450
We can account
for all the money you gave him.

957
01:07:21,540 --> 01:07:24,450
I gave him nothing
apart from his salary.

958
01:07:24,540 --> 01:07:28,050
?300,000 and?400,000 in cash.

959
01:07:28,140 --> 01:07:29,290
Huh?

960
01:07:30,100 --> 01:07:31,370
Well?

961
01:07:31,900 --> 01:07:33,380
Well, ask him.

962
01:07:33,460 --> 01:07:34,940
He forged my signature.

963
01:07:35,020 --> 01:07:36,890
On your instructions

964
01:07:36,980 --> 01:07:40,010
so that you could distance yourself
from the money, is that not so?

965
01:07:40,100 --> 01:07:41,450
No.

966
01:07:41,860 --> 01:07:45,130
Isn't it also true
you used the money for a bribe?

967
01:07:46,660 --> 01:07:48,090
I know nothing of any bribe.

968
01:07:48,180 --> 01:07:51,210
Isn't it true
that you bribed a cabinet minister?

969
01:07:58,700 --> 01:08:01,210
You needn't answer
that question if you feel

970
01:08:01,300 --> 01:08:03,530
that it might incriminate you.

971
01:08:04,380 --> 01:08:07,330
Well, it certainly will
if I don't answer it.

972
01:08:08,740 --> 01:08:11,570
Mr Cantwell,
your client is a total fantasist.

973
01:08:11,660 --> 01:08:13,210
And isn't it true that these payments

974
01:08:13,300 --> 01:08:16,450
were for helping facilitate
double and triple billing

975
01:08:16,540 --> 01:08:20,890
for equipment on defence contracts
that were ludicrously over budget?

976
01:08:21,620 --> 01:08:24,210
- Total garbage.
- Sir, I ask you again.

977
01:08:25,100 --> 01:08:28,170
Were the two cash withdrawals
on your account

978
01:08:28,620 --> 01:08:34,650
for?300,000 and?400,000,
Lines 17 and 24 on the statement,

979
01:08:34,740 --> 01:08:37,200
money to bribe a cabinet minister?

980
01:08:39,020 --> 01:08:40,050
No.

981
01:08:40,700 --> 01:08:43,490
And whoever told you that
is a total liar.

982
01:08:44,500 --> 01:08:48,250
Oh, it is you who has the record
for lies and deception.

983
01:08:50,580 --> 01:08:52,570
Is it not, sir?

984
01:08:54,700 --> 01:08:56,930
Get Deed off this embezzlement case.

985
01:08:57,020 --> 01:08:58,890
We're trying. He doesn't respond.

986
01:08:58,980 --> 01:09:02,370
Well, this is ridiculous.
Aren't you in control of your judges?

987
01:09:02,460 --> 01:09:05,690
At this rate they'll be running
the country instead of the cabinet.

988
01:09:05,780 --> 01:09:08,050
Is the Lord Chancellor
up for Deed's public humiliation?

989
01:09:08,140 --> 01:09:10,410
Let's try the newshounds first.

990
01:09:11,340 --> 01:09:13,290
Is there nothing else in your canon?

991
01:09:13,380 --> 01:09:16,210
Only a move to split him away
from Mrs Mills.

992
01:09:16,300 --> 01:09:19,290
She is still officially
running the case.

993
01:09:32,340 --> 01:09:33,970
Thank you, Rosie.

994
01:09:38,260 --> 01:09:40,290
Two great legal minds.

995
01:09:41,340 --> 01:09:43,570
I'm optimistic of a solution.

996
01:09:46,900 --> 01:09:50,210
Neither Joe nor I can
find the answer you want, Ian.

997
01:09:51,260 --> 01:09:54,130
But Deed slept with the claimant,

998
01:09:54,860 --> 01:09:56,690
and before giving judgment.

999
01:09:56,780 --> 01:10:00,560
- That is a separate issue.
- And he gave judgment against her.

1000
01:10:01,020 --> 01:10:05,090
Perhaps she was a poor lover.
That hardly excuses him, Joe.

1001
01:10:05,180 --> 01:10:06,970
It does not.

1002
01:10:07,060 --> 01:10:09,570
This judge is completely out of control.

1003
01:10:09,660 --> 01:10:12,530
There must be some way
to bring him to account.

1004
01:10:12,620 --> 01:10:15,690
Yes, Ian. Impeach him.

1005
01:10:16,660 --> 01:10:18,020
I hardly think the Lord Chancellor

1006
01:10:18,100 --> 01:10:20,820
will welcome that degree of publicity
for the bench.

1007
01:10:20,900 --> 01:10:24,860
With what Deed is threatening to expose,
he may have no choice.

1008
01:10:39,540 --> 01:10:42,000
- Hello.
- Jo, it's me. Are you ready?

1009
01:10:43,100 --> 01:10:45,170
Sir John. Jill Miro.

1010
01:10:45,260 --> 01:10:47,055
I'm a journalist.
Do you mind if I ask you some questions?

1011
01:10:47,060 --> 01:10:48,170
Yes, I would mind.

1012
01:10:48,260 --> 01:10:50,570
Is it true you had extra-marital
relations with a woman

1013
01:10:50,660 --> 01:10:53,120
who was a claimant in your court?

1014
01:10:53,220 --> 01:10:55,170
- Did you ask the claimant?
- Yes, I did.

1015
01:10:55,260 --> 01:10:56,450
Then you have your answer.

1016
01:10:56,540 --> 01:10:59,330
Perhaps you'd like to
set the record straight, Sir John.

1017
01:10:59,420 --> 01:11:02,210
All right.
Extra-martial means adulterous.

1018
01:11:02,300 --> 01:11:04,450
Adultery is voluntary sexual intercourse

1019
01:11:04,540 --> 01:11:06,660
between a married man
and a woman who is not his wife.

1020
01:11:06,750 --> 01:11:08,790
- I'm not married.
- But you shouldn't have done it.

1021
01:11:08,795 --> 01:11:11,055
It seems you've written your story.

1022
01:11:11,700 --> 01:11:12,970
Sorry about all this.

1023
01:11:13,060 --> 01:11:15,170
- Feeling any better?
- A bit.

1024
01:11:15,340 --> 01:11:16,740
Little by little, huh?

1025
01:11:16,820 --> 01:11:19,170
Sir John, did you have an affair
with Morag Hughes

1026
01:11:19,260 --> 01:11:21,650
at the Judges' Seminar in Warwick?

1027
01:11:26,100 --> 01:11:28,010
Any comment, Sir John?

1028
01:11:32,500 --> 01:11:34,490
Sir John, any comment?

1029
01:11:38,780 --> 01:11:40,740
Would you believe me
if I told you it wasn't true?

1030
01:11:40,830 --> 01:11:42,620
I'd be obliged to.
You're a High Court judge.

1031
01:11:42,710 --> 01:11:45,410
She was a plant.
I spotted her a mile off.

1032
01:11:45,980 --> 01:11:48,730
I think Laurence James put her on to me.

1033
01:11:52,580 --> 01:11:54,810
I don't know
where I fit into your life, John.

1034
01:11:54,900 --> 01:11:57,360
All that seems to drive you
is the perpetual struggle

1035
01:11:57,460 --> 01:12:00,570
against the club
that you so much want to be in.

1036
01:12:02,740 --> 01:12:03,850
John.

1037
01:12:05,820 --> 01:12:09,410
I've heard the DCA are intending
to impeach you.

1038
01:12:11,100 --> 01:12:12,580
Surprise me.

1039
01:12:13,020 --> 01:12:15,410
They're going to offer you a way out.

1040
01:12:15,500 --> 01:12:17,730
As shabby as this is,

1041
01:12:17,820 --> 01:12:20,570
you might be advised to take it.

1042
01:12:34,260 --> 01:12:38,170
Your Honour, the prosecution declines
to go on with this case.

1043
01:12:56,500 --> 01:12:58,410
John, can they do this?

1044
01:13:03,620 --> 01:13:05,570
John, what should I do?

1045
01:13:14,140 --> 01:13:15,970
This isn't acceptable.

1046
01:13:25,820 --> 01:13:28,850
I think it best
if I direct the jury to acquit.

1047
01:13:31,460 --> 01:13:32,570
No.

1048
01:13:32,660 --> 01:13:35,610
Mr Sorrell, you've closed your case.

1049
01:13:35,700 --> 01:13:38,340
Mr Cantwell should have
the opportunity to present his.

1050
01:13:38,420 --> 01:13:42,380
But we would argue for a dismissal.
There is no case to answer.

1051
01:13:42,740 --> 01:13:45,330
That's not as I read it, Mr Cantwell.

1052
01:13:58,460 --> 01:14:00,490
Let's have the jury back.

1053
01:14:03,700 --> 01:14:06,210
Then I intend to call Rufus Barron.

1054
01:14:15,540 --> 01:14:16,940
Mr Barron,

1055
01:14:17,620 --> 01:14:19,290
can you tell the court

1056
01:14:19,380 --> 01:14:23,570
how?3.7 million came to be
in your personal account?

1057
01:14:25,020 --> 01:14:28,090
I took it out of Tim's account
and put it into my account.

1058
01:14:28,180 --> 01:14:30,050
Why did you do that?

1059
01:14:30,140 --> 01:14:32,290
I believed I was going off
to a new life with Tim.

1060
01:14:32,380 --> 01:14:34,090
This is rubbish!

1061
01:14:34,180 --> 01:14:35,690
I'm sorry, Tim.

1062
01:14:35,780 --> 01:14:39,370
Did you have any sort of relationship
with Tim Listfield

1063
01:14:39,460 --> 01:14:42,130
other than employer/employee?

1064
01:14:42,220 --> 01:14:43,290
Yes.

1065
01:14:44,300 --> 01:14:47,210
He plucked me out of
the accounts department of Whittakers.

1066
01:14:47,300 --> 01:14:48,650
We'd met at the Christmas party.

1067
01:14:48,740 --> 01:14:50,220
It's all lies.

1068
01:14:51,260 --> 01:14:55,410
- Did he make you any promises?
- He said he found me very personable.

1069
01:14:56,220 --> 01:14:58,340
As we got closer he said he knew
where this was going.

1070
01:14:58,380 --> 01:14:59,810
We couldn't fight it.

1071
01:14:59,900 --> 01:15:01,810
Did Listfield fight it?

1072
01:15:03,540 --> 01:15:05,050
No, he didn't.

1073
01:15:05,940 --> 01:15:07,930
He didn't want to.

1074
01:15:08,260 --> 01:15:11,770
He was going through
such a terrible time with his wife.

1075
01:15:12,180 --> 01:15:15,330
People think he's just a ruthless
businessman, but he's not.

1076
01:15:19,020 --> 01:15:21,690
I've seen him at his most vulnerable.

1077
01:15:23,300 --> 01:15:25,050
Thank you.

1078
01:15:28,500 --> 01:15:31,090
Why are you here, Mr Barron?

1079
01:15:32,140 --> 01:15:34,090
I don't understand the question.

1080
01:15:34,180 --> 01:15:36,210
Why are you standing trial

1081
01:15:36,300 --> 01:15:38,940
instead of living the life of luxury
with Tim Listfield

1082
01:15:39,020 --> 01:15:40,890
with whom you say you had an affair?

1083
01:15:40,980 --> 01:15:43,050
I'd put on a lot of weight.

1084
01:15:43,860 --> 01:15:46,050
One day he just said,
"You're too fat for me."

1085
01:15:46,140 --> 01:15:47,540
You're too fat?

1086
01:15:47,620 --> 01:15:49,530
It was very, very hurtful.

1087
01:15:49,620 --> 01:15:52,370
This decent,
hardworking businessman

1088
01:15:52,460 --> 01:15:54,530
just left you
with all his money, did he?

1089
01:15:54,620 --> 01:15:56,490
No, he put the police onto me.

1090
01:15:56,580 --> 01:15:58,930
You betrayed his trust.
You stole from him.

1091
01:15:59,020 --> 01:16:00,690
No, he gave me the money.

1092
01:16:00,780 --> 01:16:04,410
Mr Barron, you're a fantasist.
This whole story,

1093
01:16:05,860 --> 01:16:09,050
the love affair, the castle in Spain,

1094
01:16:09,140 --> 01:16:11,500
Tim Listfield telling you
to put the money into your account

1095
01:16:11,540 --> 01:16:14,570
to keep it from his divorcing wife
is a lie, isn't it?

1096
01:16:14,660 --> 01:16:17,010
- A fantasy.
- No, it's all true.

1097
01:16:17,100 --> 01:16:20,450
The facts are, Mr Barron,
that you placed bank transfers

1098
01:16:20,540 --> 01:16:22,970
made out either to cash
or bogus concerns

1099
01:16:23,060 --> 01:16:28,010
in front of your busy, trusting boss
and he signed without close attention.

1100
01:16:28,580 --> 01:16:32,330
You repeatedly siphoned his money
into your account,

1101
01:16:32,420 --> 01:16:34,690
sometimes forging
Sir Tim Listfield's signature.

1102
01:16:34,780 --> 01:16:36,770
No, it's not true.

1103
01:16:36,860 --> 01:16:38,580
Tim Listfield never so much
as looked at you

1104
01:16:38,585 --> 01:16:40,890
with any sexual connotation, did he?

1105
01:16:40,980 --> 01:16:43,370
He did. He did, he loved me.

1106
01:16:44,260 --> 01:16:46,010
Are you telling this jury

1107
01:16:46,100 --> 01:16:48,660
that a man whose name has been
connected romantically

1108
01:16:48,740 --> 01:16:52,210
with some of the world's
most beautiful, most glamorous women

1109
01:16:52,300 --> 01:16:55,020
was only pretending to be heterosexual?

1110
01:16:56,500 --> 01:16:59,650
The fact is, your humble job

1111
01:16:59,740 --> 01:17:02,610
brought you into contact
with the super rich

1112
01:17:02,700 --> 01:17:05,420
and you thought
you should be super rich.

1113
01:17:05,500 --> 01:17:10,090
But instead of earning your riches, you
chose to steal them from your employer,

1114
01:17:10,180 --> 01:17:13,890
then make up cruel, hurtful lies
to disguise what you are.

1115
01:17:15,420 --> 01:17:17,930
A thief and a liar

1116
01:17:18,020 --> 01:17:20,770
with no regard whatsoever
for Tim Listfield's feelings.

1117
01:17:20,860 --> 01:17:22,970
- That's not true.
- It's exactly true.

1118
01:17:23,060 --> 01:17:25,490
There can be no other explanation.

1119
01:17:25,580 --> 01:17:28,330
Sir Tim Listfield is
a knight of the realm,

1120
01:17:28,420 --> 01:17:31,140
a provider of thousands of jobs,

1121
01:17:31,220 --> 01:17:32,810
a wealth creator,

1122
01:17:32,900 --> 01:17:34,490
a decent, honourable man.

1123
01:17:34,580 --> 01:17:37,850
What about the cash he made me get
to bribe people?

1124
01:17:42,980 --> 01:17:44,490
Including people in government.

1125
01:17:44,580 --> 01:17:47,490
- Well, this is another fantasy.
- It's the absolute truth.

1126
01:17:47,580 --> 01:17:51,460
Mr Barron, do you have evidence
of the people who were bribed?

1127
01:17:52,100 --> 01:17:53,320
Look at the statements.

1128
01:17:53,420 --> 01:17:55,930
Stop this now
or it could get completely out of hand.

1129
01:17:56,020 --> 01:17:58,580
No, it would look as if
we're suppressing sensitive evidence.

1130
01:17:58,660 --> 01:17:59,980
Mr Barron.

1131
01:18:00,100 --> 01:18:03,690
Item 13, the statement, Line 27,

1132
01:18:04,140 --> 01:18:07,010
the withdrawal of?100,000 in cash.

1133
01:18:09,100 --> 01:18:13,060
That was a payment to two officials
in the Department of Trade.

1134
01:18:14,420 --> 01:18:16,810
Yes. Why were they being bribed?

1135
01:18:17,460 --> 01:18:21,210
To help pass double and triple billing
on defence equipment.

1136
01:18:22,740 --> 01:18:25,090
He also gave a minister of state

1137
01:18:26,260 --> 01:18:30,300
?700,000 in cash
on two separate occasions

1138
01:18:31,140 --> 01:18:32,810
to accept his company's over-runs

1139
01:18:32,900 --> 01:18:35,650
on their original estimates
for radar equipment.

1140
01:18:35,740 --> 01:18:38,130
What were these, Mr Barron?

1141
01:18:42,860 --> 01:18:45,810
The company estimated?680 million

1142
01:18:45,900 --> 01:18:48,930
to develop a new radar system
for the navy.

1143
01:18:50,820 --> 01:18:53,280
It went over budget by?700 million,

1144
01:18:53,380 --> 01:18:55,570
due almost entirely
to double and triple billing.

1145
01:18:55,660 --> 01:18:57,330
- That's a lie!
- Silence.

1146
01:18:57,420 --> 01:18:59,930
They were extra development costs.

1147
01:19:00,500 --> 01:19:02,130
Thank you, Usher.

1148
01:19:02,220 --> 01:19:04,410
Do you have anything
to substantiate this?

1149
01:19:04,500 --> 01:19:05,610
Yes.

1150
01:19:07,740 --> 01:19:10,050
I have photocopies of every extra bill.

1151
01:19:12,220 --> 01:19:16,290
Things that were paid for twice
and three times over by taxpayers.

1152
01:19:18,580 --> 01:19:21,770
He bribed the minister to sign off
on these extra charges.

1153
01:19:21,860 --> 01:19:24,930
Line 17 and 24 on the statement,

1154
01:19:26,260 --> 01:19:30,300
a?300,000 and a?400,000
cash withdrawal a month apart,

1155
01:19:32,300 --> 01:19:34,730
which he made me sign cheques for.

1156
01:19:39,300 --> 01:19:41,090
Where are these details?

1157
01:19:41,180 --> 01:19:43,570
My instructing solicitor
has gone to collect them

1158
01:19:43,660 --> 01:19:45,610
from Mr Barron's mother's house.

1159
01:19:45,700 --> 01:19:47,610
Thank you, Mr Cantwell.

1160
01:19:51,020 --> 01:19:52,970
Who was the minister?

1161
01:20:16,980 --> 01:20:18,300
Neil Haughton.

1162
01:20:19,860 --> 01:20:22,370
But he named the current Home Secretary.

1163
01:20:22,900 --> 01:20:24,220
It's totally libellous.

1164
01:20:24,300 --> 01:20:26,410
I'll sue anyone who prints
one word of it.

1165
01:20:26,500 --> 01:20:27,690
What's our legal system worth

1166
01:20:27,780 --> 01:20:30,770
if anyone can be libelled
and with no redress?

1167
01:20:31,220 --> 01:20:32,410
The PM will have Deed's guts.

1168
01:20:41,380 --> 01:20:42,380
Mrs Channing.

1169
01:20:43,460 --> 01:20:46,180
- What the hell are you doing?
- Mrs Channing, my lord.

1170
01:20:46,260 --> 01:20:47,780
You should never have let that happen.

1171
01:20:47,785 --> 01:20:50,340
- It's your way of getting back at Neil.
- No such thing.

1172
01:20:50,420 --> 01:20:53,930
He couldn't defend himself.
You should have defended him.

1173
01:20:54,020 --> 01:20:56,530
He could apply to make
a statement in open court.

1174
01:20:56,620 --> 01:20:59,970
- It warrants a judicial enquiry.
- Oh, with you heading it?

1175
01:21:00,060 --> 01:21:03,050
What are you trying to do?
Destroy Neil's career?

1176
01:21:03,140 --> 01:21:04,730
It's so mean-minded.

1177
01:21:04,820 --> 01:21:06,820
I was never that, George.
If there isn't an inquiry

1178
01:21:06,825 --> 01:21:08,140
it will look like a cover-up.

1179
01:21:08,220 --> 01:21:09,890
There's nothing to cover up.

1180
01:21:09,980 --> 01:21:11,810
Neil didn't take Listfield's money.

1181
01:21:11,900 --> 01:21:13,170
How do you know?

1182
01:21:13,260 --> 01:21:14,580
How do you know, George?

1183
01:21:14,660 --> 01:21:16,170
They go way back before you.

1184
01:21:16,260 --> 01:21:17,890
That doesn't make them corrupt.

1185
01:21:17,980 --> 01:21:21,050
Look, I know Neil.
He's worth over 70 million.

1186
01:21:21,340 --> 01:21:24,650
Why would he risk his position,
his credibility, his liberty?

1187
01:21:24,740 --> 01:21:27,410
Because he thinks he won't get caught.

1188
01:21:27,500 --> 01:21:29,140
Why do you think
he brought your father in

1189
01:21:29,145 --> 01:21:31,330
on the One-Way shares scam?

1190
01:21:31,420 --> 01:21:33,250
End this now. Stop the trial.

1191
01:21:33,340 --> 01:21:34,340
Or what?

1192
01:21:34,420 --> 01:21:36,050
I get pushed out of a window?

1193
01:21:36,140 --> 01:21:37,970
- It didn't happen.
- No?

1194
01:21:38,740 --> 01:21:40,530
I know who I believe.

1195
01:21:49,980 --> 01:21:53,010
Mr Cantwell,
where is your instructing solicitor

1196
01:21:53,100 --> 01:21:55,170
and his startling evidence?

1197
01:21:55,260 --> 01:21:58,130
Regrettably, my lord,
it wasn't to be found.

1198
01:22:00,420 --> 01:22:02,330
Do the diaries actually exist?

1199
01:22:02,420 --> 01:22:04,450
Mr Barron insists they do.

1200
01:22:05,180 --> 01:22:09,060
He said they showed minute details
of meetings with the people

1201
01:22:09,260 --> 01:22:12,530
he says were bribed by Listfield.

1202
01:22:13,900 --> 01:22:15,090
All the meetings corresponded

1203
01:22:15,180 --> 01:22:17,820
with large sums of money
withdrawn in cash.

1204
01:22:18,060 --> 01:22:20,330
Well, he is a fantasist, Brian.

1205
01:22:20,420 --> 01:22:24,250
Without any evidence
this is all just speculation, John.

1206
01:22:26,380 --> 01:22:30,930
Is there evidence that Listfield had
homosexual relations with the defendant?

1207
01:22:32,700 --> 01:22:34,180
Only Barron's word.

1208
01:22:34,260 --> 01:22:37,170
My client was married three times.

1209
01:22:37,580 --> 01:22:40,370
A new lady caused his latest divorce,

1210
01:22:40,460 --> 01:22:41,780
not a man.

1211
01:22:45,300 --> 01:22:47,860
Possibly Mr Barron is a fantasist.

1212
01:22:47,940 --> 01:22:50,810
We have to let the jury
take a view on that.

1213
01:22:51,540 --> 01:22:54,050
That would be to risk reputations

1214
01:22:54,140 --> 01:22:57,170
that do not deserve
to be put at risk, my lord.

1215
01:22:57,740 --> 01:23:01,650
Listfield, civil servants,
even the Home Secretary.

1216
01:23:02,020 --> 01:23:04,290
All on the uncorroborated story

1217
01:23:04,380 --> 01:23:07,050
from a man who seems unable
to tell fact from fiction.

1218
01:23:07,380 --> 01:23:10,450
The alternative would shriek cover-up,
wouldn't it, Ian?

1219
01:23:14,740 --> 01:23:16,450
It's your call, Jo.

1220
01:23:19,300 --> 01:23:23,970
I would like all the evidence
thoroughly examined and investigated.

1221
01:23:24,460 --> 01:23:28,240
However, you are not trying anyone
other than the defendant.

1222
01:23:29,500 --> 01:23:32,100
You have heard all sorts of allegations
against the Home Secretary

1223
01:23:32,105 --> 01:23:34,290
and Sir Tim Listfield.

1224
01:23:34,380 --> 01:23:37,130
Allegations are not evidence.

1225
01:23:37,780 --> 01:23:42,250
On the other hand, where you believe
that an allegation is supported

1226
01:23:42,340 --> 01:23:45,610
then you may act
if you find that it's relevant.

1227
01:23:46,820 --> 01:23:50,050
Remember, the defendant does not
have to prove that he is innocent.

1228
01:23:50,140 --> 01:23:52,650
The prosecution must prove his guilt.

1229
01:23:54,700 --> 01:23:58,010
Now, would you please retire
and consider your verdict?

1230
01:24:09,980 --> 01:24:14,490
- These are only photocopies, Steve.
- He must have the diaries well hidden.

1231
01:24:18,780 --> 01:24:20,770
The girls will find them.

1232
01:24:27,100 --> 01:24:28,730
Stand up, please.

1233
01:24:31,620 --> 01:24:34,080
Will the jury foreman please stand?

1234
01:24:37,180 --> 01:24:39,970
On the first count on the indictment,

1235
01:24:40,980 --> 01:24:43,850
obtaining property by deception,

1236
01:24:44,540 --> 01:24:49,740
how do you find Rufus Barron?
Guilty or not guilty?

1237
01:24:54,860 --> 01:24:56,210
Not guilty.

1238
01:25:05,820 --> 01:25:07,140
Excuse me.

1239
01:25:07,580 --> 01:25:09,370
Congratulations again, Rufus.

1240
01:25:09,460 --> 01:25:12,020
Not only are you a free man,
you're also a rich one.

1241
01:25:12,220 --> 01:25:13,980
Tim will never forgive me
for what I've done.

1242
01:25:13,985 --> 01:25:15,815
Oh, get real, Rufus.

1243
01:25:16,460 --> 01:25:19,450
There was no love affair, was there?

1244
01:25:21,660 --> 01:25:23,650
He did ask me to hide money
from his wife.

1245
01:25:23,740 --> 01:25:28,250
But did he ask you to buy a sports car
and a home in Spain with his money?

1246
01:25:30,900 --> 01:25:33,360
- Thanks for everything, Mr Cantwell.
- Mmm-hmm.

1247
01:25:34,020 --> 01:25:37,010
Oh, you know he will sue you
to get his money back.

1248
01:25:37,620 --> 01:25:40,010
I'll take your case on, for cash.

1249
01:25:45,140 --> 01:25:47,650
This situation can only get worse.

1250
01:25:47,740 --> 01:25:50,170
Not only is Deed pushing
for a judicial inquiry

1251
01:25:50,260 --> 01:25:52,130
into the affairs
of Haughton and Listfield,

1252
01:25:52,220 --> 01:25:53,410
he has the civil action

1253
01:25:53,500 --> 01:25:56,290
involving Cardinal Waste Management PLC.

1254
01:25:56,860 --> 01:25:59,530
It's a sister company of Listfield's.

1255
01:25:59,980 --> 01:26:02,650
You can't take the case away from him
now he's started it.

1256
01:26:02,740 --> 01:26:04,810
We can, Monty, and we will.

1257
01:26:04,900 --> 01:26:06,810
You must wrest it back.

1258
01:26:07,580 --> 01:26:09,410
I will not.

1259
01:26:11,460 --> 01:26:14,610
Then we will draft in
Michael Niven to do so.

1260
01:26:19,660 --> 01:26:21,210
Ah, Mimi.

1261
01:26:24,420 --> 01:26:27,370
Mrs Mills,
might I have a word with John?

1262
01:26:28,140 --> 01:26:29,490
Of course.

1263
01:26:32,380 --> 01:26:34,810
You were quite right
to resist that offer.

1264
01:26:34,900 --> 01:26:37,250
It was scandalously political.

1265
01:26:39,540 --> 01:26:41,540
It's beginning to feel as though
we are all working

1266
01:26:41,545 --> 01:26:43,975
for Her Majesty's Government PLC.

1267
01:26:46,100 --> 01:26:47,610
Just be careful.

1268
01:26:47,700 --> 01:26:49,180
Thanks, Monty.

1269
01:27:00,780 --> 01:27:04,450
He hopes you'll consider
sitting full time as a judge, Jo.

1270
01:27:05,100 --> 01:27:06,500
It gets better and better.

1271
01:27:06,580 --> 01:27:09,140
John, nobody believes what happened.

1272
01:27:10,060 --> 01:27:11,210
I do.

